select 'd43c3d57-8564-5cce-97c6-98ae30dbfe84'::uuid, 'conditions-of-use', '1.0', 1, 0, 0, '2026-12-01'::date, 'CURRENT', true,
       '{"en": "# Conditions of Use\n\n## Agreement\n\nThese Conditions of Use (\"Conditions\") are a contract between you and [[LEGAL: Q01 legal entity name, form and state of organisation, for example \"AfroTransact, Inc., a ___ corporation\"]] (\"AfroTransact\", \"we\", \"us\"). They apply to the AfroTransact websites, the customer and driver mobile apps, text and WhatsApp messaging, and any other service that links to them (together, the \"Services\").\n\nBy creating an account, placing an order, booking a service, buying a gift card or joining a membership, you agree to these Conditions and to the policies they point to. If you do not agree, please do not use the Services.\n\nSome parts of the Services have their own terms. They are part of this agreement and are listed under \"Other terms that apply to you\" below. If one of them conflicts with these Conditions for that part of the Services, the more specific terms win.\n\n## Who we are and how to reach us\n\nAddress: {address}. Phone: {phone}. Legal notices: {legal}. Privacy questions: {privacy}. Accessibility: {accessibility}.\n\n[[LEGAL: Q02 registered agent and the address for formal legal notices]]\n\n## Other terms that apply to you\n\n- Privacy Notice, Cookie Notice and Your Privacy Choices\n- Returns, Refunds and Problems With Your Order\n- SMS and Notification Terms\n- Gift Card Terms\n- Store Credit Terms\n- Plus Membership Terms\n- Referral Program Terms\n- Pre-order and Delivery Run Terms\n- Community Guidelines\n- Prohibited and Restricted Items\n- Intellectual Property and Copyright Policy\n- Accessibility Statement\n\n## Changes to these Conditions\n\nWe may change these Conditions as the Services or the law change. For material changes we will give you at least 30 days'' notice by email and in the app before the change takes effect, except where a change is needed sooner for legal reasons or to protect people from harm. The version number and effective date are shown at the top of this page. If you keep using the Services after a change takes effect, you accept it. If you do not accept it, you can close your account before the effective date. A change never applies to an order you already placed. [[LEGAL: Q19 confirm the notice period and how acceptance of changes works]]\n\n## Who you are buying from\n\nAfroTransact is a marketplace. Two kinds of businesses sell on it.\n\n- **AfroTransact Retail.** Items shown as \"Sold by AfroTransact\" are sold by us, from our own inventory. For those items we are the seller.\n- **Independent sellers and service providers.** Many products are sold by independent sellers, and many services are performed by independent providers. The seller or provider is shown on every listing, order and receipt. They are responsible for their listings, their goods and their services. We provide the platform, take payment, can arrange delivery, and handle support and disputes.\n\nA seller or provider is not our employee or agent. Where a seller keeps stock with us (fulfilment by AfroTransact) or we deliver the order, we handle the delivery, but the seller is still the seller of the goods.\n\n## Your account\n\nYou must be at least 18 years old and able to form a binding contract to hold an account. [[LEGAL: Q10 confirm the minimum age and whether accounts for 13 to 17 year olds with a parent are allowed]] Give us accurate information and keep it up to date. Keep your password, one-time codes and sign-in methods secret. You are responsible for what happens on your account, so tell us straight away at {legal} if you think someone else has used it.\n\nOne person may hold customer, seller and provider roles on the same account. The seller and provider roles have their own agreement.\n\nYou may not share an account, sell or transfer it, or create accounts to avoid a suspension or a limit on a program (for example, to collect more than one referral reward).\n\n## Prices, payment and taxes\n\nAll prices are in US dollars (USD). The price on the product page, with any discount, is what you pay for the goods. Delivery or shipping fees, sales tax and any other charge are shown before you place the order. Fees depend on the delivery method, as explained in the Pre-order and Delivery Run Terms.\n\n**Sales tax.** We calculate sales tax from the delivery address (or, for a pickup, the pickup point) using the rates in force for that place. Where the law makes a marketplace responsible for collecting tax on sales made through it, we collect the tax from you and send it to the tax authority. The tax shown while you check out is an estimate until the order is placed; we confirm the final amount when you place the order. [[LEGAL: Q20 sales-tax wording per state, exemption certificates, and the tax treatment of delivery fees]]\n\n**When you are charged.** When you place an order, we ask your card or payment method to authorise the order total. We collect the payment for each package when it leaves for you, so a package that never ships is released rather than charged. If a package is cancelled before it leaves, the authorisation is normally released and you are not charged; if the payment was already collected, we refund it. Pre-orders and delivery runs are paid for in the same way as any other order. For services, we may charge a deposit when you book; the booking page tells you the amount before you confirm.\n\n**Payment processing by Stripe.** Card, Apple Pay, Google Pay, bank and wallet payments are processed by Stripe, Inc. and its affiliates (\"Stripe\"). When you pay or save a payment method, you agree to Stripe''s applicable terms, you acknowledge Stripe''s Privacy Policy, and you authorise us and Stripe to process the payment. Stripe may collect device and transaction data to prevent fraud and to meet its legal duties. We do not see or store your full card number. If you use Stripe''s Link service, Link may offer to remember your email, phone number and payment details across businesses; Link has its own terms and privacy notice, and using it is your choice. [[LEGAL: Q29 confirm the exact Stripe terms to name and the wording for saved methods and Link]]\n\n**Saved payment methods.** If you save a card or bank account, you authorise us to use it for purchases you make, for the Plus membership if you join it, and for any other charge you have agreed to. You can remove a saved method at any time in Your account > Payment methods. A removed method will not be used for new charges, but removing it does not cancel an order or membership already in progress; change or cancel those separately.\n\n**Failed or reversed payments.** If a payment fails or is reversed, we may cancel the order, pause your account and recover the amount you owe. Please contact us before you dispute a charge with your bank, so that we can fix a mistake quickly. You may of course exercise any rights you have with your card issuer.\n\n**Store credit and gift cards.** These are described in the Store Credit Terms and the Gift Card Terms. In short, credit can only be used to buy products and services on AfroTransact and can never be turned into cash.\n\n## Orders and cancellation\n\nAn order is an offer from you to buy. We accept it, and the contract with the seller is formed, when we confirm it. We may decline or cancel an order, for example if an item is out of stock, a price was obviously wrong, we suspect fraud, or the delivery address is outside the places we serve. If we cancel, you get a full refund of anything you paid.\n\n**Cancelling before delivery.** You can cancel an order yourself until its shipment has been prepared. After that, the order is on its way and cannot be cancelled in the app. The Returns, Refunds and Problems With Your Order page explains what to do. Services follow the provider''s cancellation policy shown before you book.\n\n## Delivery\n\nDelivery dates and delivery windows are our best estimate and are not guarantees. We tell you if a date moves. Some products are delivered by a carrier, some by AfroTransact drivers, some by the seller, and some are collected at a pickup point. Details, including delivery codes, proof of delivery and what happens if nobody can receive the package, are in the Pre-order and Delivery Run Terms. Risk of loss or damage passes to you when the package is delivered to you or to the person you named, or handed over at the pickup point. [[LEGAL: Q21 confirm the risk-of-loss wording against the law of the launch states]]\n\n## Problems with a delivered order\n\nOnce an order has been delivered, there is no self-service return or refund button. If something is wrong, go to Your account > Get help with an order, describe the problem and add photos, and our team will decide the outcome. The Returns, Refunds and Problems With Your Order page explains how this works, where refunds go and the rights the law gives you. Nothing in these Conditions removes a right you have under the law that cannot be waived.\n\n## Services and bookings\n\nWhen you book a service, the provider is responsible for performing it. Appointment times, deposits and cancellation rules are set by the provider and shown before you book. If the provider cancels or does not show up, you get a full refund, including any deposit. Providers must hold any licence the law requires for the service.\n\n## Plus membership, gift cards, store credit and referrals\n\nThese programs are optional and run under their own terms. We configure their benefits and amounts and show them in the app when you sign up or use them. We may change them for the future. A change does not take away benefits you have already earned or paid for.\n\n## Your content\n\nYou may post reviews and ratings, photos, questions, messages and other content (\"Your Content\"). You keep ownership of it. You give us a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free licence to host, show, reproduce, adapt (for example, resize or translate) and distribute Your Content in the Services and in our marketing of the Services, and to let the seller concerned show it with their listing. This licence lasts while the content is on the Services and for a reasonable time afterwards while backups and caches clear. Only post what you have the right to post. Reviews must come from a verified purchase and follow the Community Guidelines. We may remove content that breaks our rules or the law.\n\n## Messages, notifications and Lola\n\nBy creating an account you agree that we may send you service messages about your account, orders, deliveries, bookings, payments and security by email, push notification and, if you give us a mobile number and opt in, SMS and WhatsApp. Marketing messages are sent only with your separate, express consent, which is never a condition of buying anything. How to stop messages is explained in the SMS and Notification Terms. SMS program name: {smsProgramName}. Message frequency varies. Message and data rates may apply. Reply STOP to cancel and HELP for help. Carriers are not liable for delayed or undelivered messages.\n\nLola is our AI shopping assistant. Lola can make mistakes, may give out-of-date information and is not a person. Check important details such as price, delivery date, allergens and ingredients on the product page. Lola does not give medical, legal, tax or financial advice. We may ask you to confirm important actions that Lola takes for you, such as changing delivery instructions. See the Privacy Notice for how Lola uses data and the Community Guidelines for how to use it. [[LEGAL: Q16 AI disclosure wording required by state law]]\n\n## Acceptable use\n\nDo not use the Services to break the law; to harm or harass others; to place orders with stolen or unauthorised payment methods; to abuse promotions, credit, gift cards, referrals or the help process; to buy in bulk for resale where we have set a limit; to interfere with the security or operation of the Services; or to copy the Services with bots, scrapers or other automated tools without our written permission. Do not try to list or buy anything covered by the Prohibited and Restricted Items policy. We may limit, suspend or close an account, cancel orders and withhold program rewards where we reasonably believe these rules have been broken.\n\n## Third-party services and links\n\nThe Services rely on, and may link to, services run by other companies, for example Stripe (payments), Twilio and WhatsApp (messages), delivery carriers, address and map providers, and AI model providers. Their own terms and policies apply to your use of them. We are not responsible for sites or services we do not run. Where a third-party service is part of using AfroTransact (for example, receiving a text), we describe the relevant terms in the related policy.\n\n## Our intellectual property\n\nThe Services, including their design, software, text, graphics, logos and trademarks, belong to us or our licensors and are protected by law. You may use the Services for your own personal, non-commercial use as these Conditions allow. The Intellectual Property and Copyright Policy explains how to report copyright or trademark infringement.\n\n## Disclaimers\n\nTo the extent the law allows, the Services are provided \"as is\" and \"as available\". We do not promise that the Services will be uninterrupted or error free. Listings are provided by sellers; unless we are the seller, we do not promise that a listing is accurate or complete. Some states do not allow certain disclaimers, so some of this may not apply to you. [[LEGAL: Q06 disclaimer and implied-warranty wording suitable for each launch state]]\n\n## Limitation of liability\n\nTo the extent the law allows, we and our officers, employees and affiliates are not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential or punitive losses, or for loss of profits, data or goodwill. Our total liability to you for any claim about the Services is limited to [[LEGAL: Q06 liability cap, for example the greater of the amount you paid for the order concerned in the 12 months before the claim and a fixed sum]]. Nothing in these Conditions limits liability that the law does not allow to be limited, including for fraud, or for death or personal injury caused by negligence where that applies. [[LEGAL: Q06 carve-outs required in each launch state]]\n\n## Indemnity\n\nTo the extent the law allows, you agree to compensate us for losses we suffer because you break these Conditions or the law, or post content that infringes someone else''s rights. [[LEGAL: Q22 confirm whether a consumer indemnity is enforceable and wanted; many counsel remove it for consumers]]\n\n## Resolving disputes\n\n**Talk to us first.** Contact us at {legal} or through Your account > Get help with an order. Most issues are resolved within 48 hours, and we will try to resolve any dispute informally before either of us starts a formal case.\n\n**Arbitration and class action waiver.** [[LEGAL: Q05 arbitration clause. The earlier placeholder draft proposed binding individual arbitration under the AAA Consumer Arbitration Rules, a small-claims carve-out, a class-action waiver and a 30-day opt-out by writing to the legal address. Counsel to decide whether to use it, the administrator, fee allocation, a mass-arbitration protocol and state-law carve-outs]]\n\n**Governing law and courts.** [[LEGAL: Q03 governing law]] governs these Conditions, except where the law of the state where you live gives you rights that cannot be waived. [[LEGAL: Q04 courts and venue for claims that are not sent to arbitration or small claims]]\n\n## Ending your account\n\nYou can ask us to close your account at any time by contacting us at {legal} or through the privacy request form on the Privacy Choices page. We may suspend or close an account, with notice where the law requires it, if you break these Conditions, create risk or harm for others, or if we must by law. Closing an account does not cancel your obligations for orders already placed. Remaining store credit is handled under the Store Credit Terms, and we will tell you before a closure we start takes effect so that you can use your credit. Terms that by their nature should continue after the account closes, such as ownership, disclaimers, liability and dispute terms, do so.\n\n## General\n\nThese Conditions, with the policies they point to, are the whole agreement between you and us about the Services. If a part is found unenforceable, the rest stays in force. If we do not enforce a right, we have not given it up. You may not transfer your rights under these Conditions; we may transfer ours as part of a merger, sale or reorganisation, with notice to you. We are not responsible for delay caused by events beyond our control, such as severe weather, strikes, carrier or network failures, or payment-network outages.\n\nIf you have a disability and find any part of the Services hard to use, tell us at {accessibility}.\n\n[[LEGAL: Q01 state-specific consumer notices that must appear in the Conditions, for example the California Civil Code 1789.3 notice]]"}'::jsonb, 'First customer-facing version for launch. Replaces the placeholder draft seeded in the content service.', now(), 'legal-loader', now(), null
 where not exists (select 1 from legal_version where doc_type = 'conditions-of-use' and (major, minor, patch) >= (1, 0, 0));
