keting of the Services, and to let the seller concerned show it with their listing. This licence lasts while the content is on the Services and for a reasonable time afterwards while backups and caches clear. Only post what you have the right to post. Reviews must come from a verified purchase and follow the Community Guidelines. We may remove content that breaks our rules or the law.\n\n## Messages, notifications and Lola\n\nBy creating an account you agree that we may send you service messages about your account, orders, deliveries, bookings, payments and security by email, push notification and, if you give us a mobile number and opt in, SMS and WhatsApp. Marketing messages are sent only with your separate, express consent, which is never a condition of buying anything. How to stop messages is explained in the SMS and Notification Terms. SMS program name: {smsProgramName}. Message frequency varies. Message and data rates may apply. Reply STOP to cancel and HELP for help. Carriers are not liable for delayed or undelivered messages.\n\nLola is our AI shopping assistant. Lola can make mistakes, may give out-of-date information and is not a person. Check important details such as price, delivery date, allergens and ingredients on the product page. Lola does not give medical, legal, tax or financial advice. We may ask you to confirm important actions that Lola takes for you, such as changing delivery instructions. See the Privacy Notice for how Lola uses data and the Community Guidelines for how to use it. [[LEGAL: Q16 AI disclosure wording required by state law]]\n\n## Acceptable use\n\nDo not use the Services to break the law; to harm or harass others; to place orders with stolen or unauthorised payment methods; to abuse promotions, credit, gift cards, referrals or the help process; to buy in bulk for resale where we have set a limit; to interfere with the security or operation of the Services; or to copy the Services with bots, scrapers or other automated tools without our written permission. Do not try to list or buy anything covered by the Prohibited and Restricted Items policy. We may limit, suspend or close an account, cancel orders and withhold program rewards where we reasonably believe these rules have been broken.\n\n## Third-party services and links\n\nThe Services rely on, and may link to, services run by other companies, for example Stripe (payments), Twilio and WhatsApp (messages), delivery carriers, address and map providers, and AI model providers. Their own terms and policies apply to your use of them. We are not responsible for sites or services we do not run. Where a third-party service is part of using AfroTransact (for example, receiving a text), we describe the relevant terms in the related policy.\n\n## Our intellectual property\n\nThe Services, including their design, software, text, graphics, logos and trademarks, belong to us or our licensors and are protected by law. You may use the Services for your own personal, non-commercial use as these Conditions allow. The Intellectual Property and Copyright Policy explains how to report copyright or trademark infringement.\n\n## Disclaimers\n\nTo the extent the law allows, the Services are provided \"as is\" and \"as available\". We do not promise that the Services will be uninterrupted or error free. Listings are provided by sellers; unless we are the seller, we do not promise that a listing is accurate or complete. Some states do not allow certain disclaimers, so some of this may not apply to you. [[LEGAL: Q06 disclaimer and implied-warranty wording suitable for each launch state]]\n\n## Limitation of liability\n\nTo the extent the law allows, we and our officers, employees and affiliates are not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential or punitive losses, or for loss of profits, data or goodwill. Our total liability to you for any claim about the Services is limited to [[LEGAL: Q06 liability cap, for example the greater of the amount you paid for the order concerned in the 12 months before the claim and a fixed sum]]. Nothing in these Conditions limits liability that the law does not allow to be limited, including for fraud, or for death or personal injury caused by negligence where that applies. [[LEGAL: Q06 carve-outs required in each launch state]]\n\n## Indemnity\n\nTo the extent the law allows, you agree to compensate us for losses we suffer because you break these Conditions or the law, or post content that infringes someone else''s rights. [[LEGAL: Q22 confirm whether a consumer indemnity is enforceable and wanted; many counsel remove it for consumers]]\n\n## Resolving disputes\n\n**Talk to us first.** Contact us at {legal} or through Your account > Get help with an order. Most issues are resolved within 48 hours, and we will try to resolve any dispute informally before either of us starts a formal case.\n\n**Arbitration and class action waiver.** [[LEGAL: Q05 arbitration clause. The earlier placeholder draft proposed binding individual arbitration under the AAA Consumer Arbitration Rules, a small-claims carve-out, a class-action waiver and a 30-day opt-out by writing to the legal address. Counsel to decide whether to use it, the administrator, fee allocation, a mass-arbitration protocol and state-law carve-outs]]\n\n**Governing law and courts.** [[LEGAL: Q03 governing law]] governs these Conditions, except where the law of the state where you live gives you rights that cannot be waived. [[LEGAL: Q04 courts and venue for claims that are not sent to arbitration or small claims]]\n\n## Ending your account\n\nYou can ask us to close your account at any time by contacting us at {legal} or through the privacy request form on the Privacy Choices page. We may suspend or close an account, with notice where the law requires it, if you break these Conditions, create risk or harm for others, or if we must by law. Closing an account does not cancel your obligations for orders already placed. Remaining store credit is handled under the Store Credit Terms, and we will tell you before a closure we start takes effect so that you can use your credit. Terms that by their nature should continue after the account closes, such as ownership, disclaimers, liability and dispute terms, do so.\n\n## General\n\nThese Conditions, with the policies they point to, are the whole agreement between you and us about the Services. If a part is found unenforceable, the rest stays in force. If we do not enforce a right, we have not given it up. You may not transfer your rights under these Conditions; we may transfer ours as part of a merger, sale or reorganisation, with notice to you. We are not responsible for delay caused by events beyond our control, such as severe weather, strikes, carrier or network failures, or payment-network outages.\n\nIf you have a disability and find any part of the Services hard to use, tell us at {accessibility}.\n\n[[LEGAL: Q01 state-specific consumer notices that must appear in the Conditions, for example the California Civil Code 1789.3 notice]]"}'::jsonb, change_summary = 'First customer-facing version for launch. Replaces the placeholder draft seeded in the content service.', created_at = now(), updated_at = now()
    where doc_type = 'conditions-of-use' and (major, minor, patch) = (1, 0, 0) and status = 'CURRENT'
      and created_by in ('seed', 'legal-loader') and updated_at = created_at;

-- privacy 1.0 (effective 2026-12-01; locales: en; draft banner on)
delete from legal_version where doc_type = 'privacy' and created_by = 'seed'
    and exists (select 1 from legal_version c where c.doc_type = 'privacy' and c.status = 'CURRENT'
                and c.created_by = 'seed' and c.updated_at = c.created_at and (c.major, c.minor, c.patch) > (1, 0, 0));
update legal_version set status = 'ARCHIVED', archived_at = now(), updated_at = now()
    where doc_type = 'privacy' and status = 'CURRENT' and (major, minor, patch) < (1, 0, 0);
insert into legal_version (id, doc_type, version, major, minor, patch, effective_date, status, draft_banner, bodies,
                           change_summary, created_at, created_by, updated_at, archived_at)
select '5a087fa6-4019-5076-ac98-19d0d878ce4c'::uuid, 'privacy', '1.0', 1, 0, 0, '2026-12-01'::date, 'CURRENT', true,
       '{"en": "# Privacy Notice\n\n## Who this notice covers\n\nThis notice explains what personal information [[LEGAL: Q01 legal entity name]] (\"AfroTransact\", \"we\", \"us\") collects about you when you visit our websites, use our apps, shop with us, book a service, receive a delivery, talk to Lola, or contact us, and what we do with it. It also covers people who receive a gift card or a package ordered by someone else, and people who use a friend''s referral link.\n\nWe are the business that decides how this information is used (a \"controller\", or a \"business\" under US state privacy laws). When we process information for a seller or service provider to deliver your order, they have their own responsibilities for what we give them. Payment processors act on their own terms for some data; see \"Who we share it with\".\n\nContact: {privacy}. {address}. Phone: {phone}.\n\n## Information we collect\n\n| Category | Examples | Where it comes from |\n|---|---|---|\n| Identifiers and contact details | Name, email, phone number, delivery and billing addresses, account ID, sign-in method (including Google, Apple or Facebook sign-in if you use them) | You, your device, social sign-in |\n| Account security data | Password hash, one-time codes, two-step verification settings, device and session data | You, your device |\n| Commercial information | Orders, bookings, carts, saved items, reviews and ratings, help requests, store credit and gift card ledger entries, membership status, referral activity | You, our systems |\n| Payment information | Payment tokens, card brand, last four digits and expiry, billing postal code, refund and dispute records. Full card numbers are handled by Stripe and are not stored by us | You, Stripe |\n| Delivery information | Delivery instructions, delivery window, pickup point, delivery code, proof of delivery, driver and route events, delivery attempts | You, our drivers and carriers |\n| Location information | Address you enter or pick; your current location if you press \"Use my current location\"; approximate location from your network address | You, your device |\n| Messages and content | Messages with sellers, providers, drivers and support; photos and descriptions you send with a help request; reviews and photos; conversations with Lola | You |\n| Device and usage information | Browser, device model, app version, pages and screens viewed, search queries, errors, cookie and SDK identifiers | Your device, cookies and similar technologies (see the Cookie Notice) |\n| Marketing and consent records | Your cookie choices, email and push preferences, SMS and WhatsApp opt-in and opt-out records (what you agreed to, when, from where and the version of the text), referral code | You, our systems |\n| Inferences | Product recommendations and interests inferred from what you browse and buy, fraud and risk scores | Our systems |\n\nWe do not knowingly collect sensitive personal information such as health, biometric or precise-location history information for profiling. Precise location is used only when you press the location button, and only to fill in an address or show delivery progress. Some data you provide, for example product searches or Lola questions, could reveal something sensitive; please do not include information you do not want us to handle. [[LEGAL: Q11 confirm the sensitive-data statement, for example for precise geolocation and account credentials under CPRA]]\n\n## How we use it\n\n- **To give you what you ask for:** create your account, process orders, bookings and payments, calculate and collect sales tax, deliver packages (including to a pickup point or on a delivery run), handle cancellations, help requests and refunds, and run store credit, gift cards, Plus membership and referrals.\n- **To keep the Services safe:** prevent and investigate fraud, abuse, referral manipulation, chargebacks and unsafe listings; verify purchases for reviews; secure accounts.\n- **To communicate with you:** send order, delivery, security and account messages by email, push, SMS and WhatsApp; answer support requests; and, only with your consent, send marketing.\n- **To improve and personalise:** search, recommendations, Lola, and de-identified analytics on how the Services perform.\n- **To advertise and measure advertising,** only where you have allowed advertising cookies or SDKs, and subject to your opt-out rights (see Your Privacy Choices).\n- **To meet legal duties:** tax, accounting, sanctions and records, and to respond to lawful requests.\n\nWe rely on these legal bases where the law asks for one: performing our contract with you, our legitimate interests (security, fraud, service improvement), your consent (marketing messages, advertising cookies), and legal obligation.\n\n## Who we share it with\n\nWe share personal information only as described here.\n\n- **Sellers and providers** receive what they need to fulfil your order or booking, such as your name, delivery address or pickup point, items ordered, and messages you send them. For deliveries we handle, the seller may get only the delivery status.\n- **Delivery partners:** AfroTransact drivers, pickup-point operators and carriers (for example UPS, USPS, FedEx and DHL Express) receive the name, address, phone number and delivery instructions needed to deliver, and delivery events come back to us.\n- **Payment and fraud services:** Stripe, Inc. processes your payments, saved payment methods and Link. Stripe collects payment, device and fraud-signal data and uses it under its own privacy policy as well as on our behalf. [[LEGAL: Q29 confirm whether Stripe is a controller, processor or independent business for each use, and how to describe it]]\n- **Messaging services:** Twilio (SMS, with Amazon Web Services as a backup route), Meta''s WhatsApp Business Platform (WhatsApp), Resend and Amazon SES (email), and Google Firebase Cloud Messaging and Apple Push Notification service (push). They deliver the messages we ask them to and keep delivery records.\n- **Address, map and routing services:** Google Maps Platform (address suggestions, location lookup and drive-time routing), Smarty (US address checks) and OpenStreetMap-based services. They receive what you type into an address field, or your coordinates, and the answer comes back to us.\n- **AI services:** Lola and other AI features send your text, with personal details removed first where we can, to an AI gateway we run, which uses model providers reached through OpenRouter (for example Google and OpenAI models). See \"AI features\".\n- **Hosting and infrastructure:** cloud, database, storage and content-delivery services, including Cloudflare, Layerbase and our cloud hosting providers, and monitoring and error-tracking services such as Grafana Cloud and Sentry. They store and process data for us under contracts that limit what they can do with it.\n- **Advertising and analytics providers,** such as Google Ads and Meta, only if you allow advertising cookies. See the Cookie Notice for the exact list.\n- **Professional advisers, auditors and authorities** where the law requires or to protect rights, safety and property, and **a buyer or successor** if the business is sold or reorganised (we will tell you and honour this notice).\n- **People you choose:** for example the recipient of a gift card you send, or a friend who joined with your referral code (they see only that a referral was made, never your orders).\n\nWe do not sell personal information for money. Some advertising features may count as \"sharing\" for cross-context behavioural advertising under California law; we only enable them for people who have not opted out, and you can opt out at any time through Your Privacy Choices or a Global Privacy Control signal. [[LEGAL: Q11 confirm the sale and share characterisation of advertising cookies and the Meta and Google data flows]]\n\nA current list of our service providers is kept in the Subprocessors page. [[LEGAL: Q11 cross-check this notice against the subprocessor list]]\n\n## Mobile numbers, SMS and WhatsApp\n\nWe use your mobile number to send the order, delivery, booking, payment and security messages you asked for (including one-time passcodes) and, only if you separately opted in, marketing messages. No mobile information will be shared with third parties or affiliates for marketing or promotional purposes. Text-messaging opt-in data and consent are excluded from every sharing category in this notice and will not be shared with any third party except the service providers that deliver the messages for us, who may not use it for their own marketing. Reply STOP to any text to opt out. WhatsApp messages need their own opt-in and are covered by the SMS and Notification Terms and WhatsApp''s own terms.\n\n## AI features\n\nLola, our AI shopping assistant, and some other features (for example search, translation, listing help and image checks) use AI models.\n\n- Before a message goes to a model, we remove or mask things like email addresses, phone numbers, card numbers, government ID numbers and street addresses where we can detect them. Lola''s stored memory of a conversation is kept in the masked form.\n- We route requests to model providers through OpenRouter. We configure prompt and response logging and training off where the provider allows it, and we do not allow model providers to use your content to train their models under our agreements. Model providers may keep data for a short time to run their service or for safety. [[LEGAL: Q16 verify these statements against OpenRouter''s current terms and each routed model provider''s data policy before launch]]\n- Lola acts only on your account when you ask, and asks you to confirm important actions.\n- AI output can be wrong. We do not use Lola or other AI to make decisions about you that have legal or similarly significant effects without human review.\n- Do not put sensitive information such as health details, government ID numbers or full card numbers into a Lola chat.\n\n## Cookies and similar technologies\n\nWe use cookies, local storage, pixels and software development kits (SDKs). The Cookie Notice explains each category and lets you choose. We honour the Global Privacy Control signal as an opt-out of advertising cookies and of sale and sharing.\n\n## Reviews, public content and referrals\n\nReviews show your first name and last initial and a \"Verified purchase\" label. Photos you add to a review are public. Messages with a seller are visible to that seller and to us. Referral programs use technical signals such as a sign-up device, network, delivery address and payment-card fingerprint (in a one-way form) to detect self-referral and abuse; they are used only for that purpose.\n\n## How long we keep it\n\nWe keep order, payment, tax and credit-ledger records for 7 years for tax, accounting and legal reasons. We keep other information only as long as needed for the reason we collected it: for example, messages with support for as long as the matter is open and for a limited time afterwards, and marketing and consent records for as long as the consent is relied upon and the period afterwards in which we may need to prove it. When you close your account, we delete or de-identify your personal information within 90 days, except what the law requires us to keep, what we need to handle open orders, disputes, fraud and unpaid balances, and consent and opt-out records. [[LEGAL: Q11 confirm retention periods per data category]]\n\n## Your rights and choices\n\nDepending on where you live (for example California, Virginia, Colorado, Connecticut, Utah, Texas, Oregon and other states with a comprehensive privacy law), you may have the right to:\n\n- know and access the personal information we hold about you;\n- correct it, delete it, or get a portable copy;\n- opt out of sale, sharing and targeted advertising, and of profiling that produces significant effects;\n- limit the use of sensitive personal information (we use it only for the purposes the law allows);\n- appeal a decision on your request; and\n- not be treated worse for exercising these rights.\n\nThe page Your Privacy Choices explains how to make a request, how we verify it, how an authorised agent can act for you, and how to appeal. You can also email {privacy}. Residents of California can ask once a year which categories of personal information we shared with third parties for their direct marketing; we do not share it for that purpose. California residents under 18 who are registered users can ask us to remove content they posted.\n\n## Children\n\nAfroTransact is for adults and is not directed to children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13 and will delete it if we learn we have. [[LEGAL: Q10 age wording, teens 13 to 17 and any state minor-data rules]]\n\n## Security\n\nWe use encryption in transit and at rest, role-based and logged access, and separate storage for identity documents. Payment card data is handled by Stripe, which is certified to PCI DSS Level 1. No system is perfectly secure; if we learn of a breach that affects you, we will tell you as the law requires.\n\n## Where your data is stored\n\nWe store and process data in the United States. Some service providers may process it in other countries under contracts that protect it. [[LEGAL: Q28 confirm transfer wording; the launch is US-only but diaspora customers may travel or live abroad]]\n\n## Changes to this notice\n\nIf we make material changes we will tell you by email or in the app at least 30 days before they take effect, as far as the law lets us. The version and effective date are at the top of this page.\n\n## Contact us\n\nEmail {privacy}. Write to {address}. Phone {phone}. If you have a disability and need this notice in another format, email {accessibility}. [[LEGAL: Q02 contact details and any required state-specific contact methods, such as a toll-free number for requests]]"}'::jsonb, 'First customer-facing version for launch. Adds store credit, gift cards, membership, referrals, delivery runs, WhatsApp, Lola and the named service-provider categories.', now(), 'legal-loader', now(), null
 where not exists (select 1 from legal_version where doc_type = 'privacy' and (major, minor, patch) >= (1, 0, 0));
update legal_version set effective_date = '2026-12-01'::date, draft_banner = true,
