                           change_summary, created_at, created_by, updated_at, archived_at)
select '28b5079b-d23a-565c-bbf4-ce63ec8adddc'::uuid, 'sms-terms', '1.0', 1, 0, 0, '2026-12-01'::date, 'CURRENT', true,
       '{"en": "# SMS and Notification Terms\n\n## Program\n\n{smsProgramName} is a text-message program from [[LEGAL: Q01 legal entity name]] (\"AfroTransact\", \"we\"). [[LEGAL: Q14 program name, brand name as registered for A2P 10DLC or toll-free verification, and the sending number or short code to publish here]]\n\nThere are two kinds of messages, and you agree to them separately.\n\n**1. Account and order messages (recurring, automated).** These are sent because of something you did or asked for. They include: order confirmations; pre-order and delivery run updates for your own orders (including cutoff reminders, confirmation or cancellation); shipping, driver and delivery updates, delivery codes and delivery-attempt notices; booking reminders and changes; payment, refund and store credit notices; help request updates; security alerts; and one-time passcodes that you request.\n\n**2. Marketing messages (AfroTransact Deals).** If you separately opt in, we also send offers, restock alerts, pre-order and delivery run announcements, and membership or referral promotions. Opting in is optional.\n\n## How you opt in\n\n- **Account and order messages:** you opt in by entering your mobile number and ticking the SMS consent box at sign-up, checkout, booking or in Your account > Notifications, or by texting START to our number. We confirm your enrolment by text.\n- **Marketing messages:** you opt in with a separate, unticked box that is only about marketing texts, or by texting the keyword shown in an offer. You can use the service and buy things without ticking it.\n- **WhatsApp:** you opt in to WhatsApp messages separately, naming WhatsApp, in the same places. Agreeing to SMS does not opt you in to WhatsApp, and agreeing to WhatsApp does not opt you in to SMS.\n\nThe consent text shown next to the box is:\n\n> By checking this box, you agree to receive recurring automated texts from {smsProgramName} at the number above. Consent is not a condition of purchase. Message frequency varies. Msg & data rates may apply. Reply STOP to cancel, HELP for help. See the SMS Terms and Privacy Notice.\n\nMarketing consent text names the brand, says the messages are marketing and repeats the frequency, rates, STOP and HELP wording. Your agreement is **not a condition of buying any product or service**.\n\n## Message frequency\n\nMessage frequency varies with your orders, bookings and activity. For marketing messages, we send up to 4 messages a month. [[LEGAL: Q14 confirm the marketing frequency cap]]\n\n## Message and data rates\n\nMessage and data rates may apply according to your mobile plan. We do not charge for texts. Your mobile carrier may.\n\n## Opting out and getting help\n\n- **Stop:** reply **STOP**, **END**, **CANCEL**, **UNSUBSCRIBE** or **QUIT** to any text. We also treat STOPALL, OPTOUT and REVOKE as opt-outs. You get one final text confirming it and no further messages. Replying STOP to a marketing text stops marketing texts; replying STOP to an account message text stops all texts to that number from this program. You can also turn texts off in Your account > Notifications.\n- **Rejoin:** reply **START** (or UNSTOP or YES) to the same number, or opt in again in your account.\n- **Help:** reply **HELP**, call {phone} or write to {privacy}.\n- **Security codes:** if you opt out of SMS, we will send security codes and sign-in codes by email or another method you have set up instead. If you have no other method, you may not be able to use sign-in methods that need a text.\n- **WhatsApp:** reply STOP in the chat, block the business, or turn it off in Your account > Notifications. We will stop WhatsApp messages. Your SMS choices are not changed.\n\nIf you change your mobile number, tell us. A new owner of your old number may reply STOP or HELP, and we will honour it for that number.\n\n## Supported carriers\n\nSupported on major US carriers including AT&T, T-Mobile, Verizon and their virtual operators. **Carriers are not liable for delayed or undelivered messages.** Delivery depends on your carrier, your phone, your coverage and your settings, so we cannot guarantee that every message arrives, or that it arrives on time.\n\n## Quiet hours\n\nWe hold marketing and other non-urgent messages between 9 pm and 8 am in your local time and send them after 8 am. You can set quieter hours of your own in Your account > Notifications. Delivery and security messages, and one-time passcodes, may be sent at any time. [[LEGAL: Q14 the platform default is quiet hours from 21:00 to 08:00 local and this text now matches it; check state telemarketing laws that allow a shorter window, such as Florida, Oklahoma, Maryland and Washington, and set stricter quiet hours for those states if needed]]\n\n## Who sends and who sees\n\nOur messaging providers, such as Twilio (and Amazon Web Services as a backup route), carry the messages. They may see the message content and your number so that they can deliver, and they may not use them for their own marketing. WhatsApp messages are carried by WhatsApp (Meta), which has its own terms and privacy policy. WhatsApp messages from businesses are sent only from message templates approved by WhatsApp, and WhatsApp may process the content under its own policies. [[LEGAL: Q15 WhatsApp Business account name, the number we message from, whether WhatsApp is switched on at launch (it is off by default), and the exact WhatsApp opt-in wording]]\n\n## Consent records\n\nWe keep a record of your consent: the phone number, the date and time, how and where you opted in (for example the sign-up page or an in-app screen), the exact wording and version of the consent text you saw, your choices about each kind of message, and any later opt-out or opt-in, so that we can show that you agreed and honour what you chose. We keep this for as long as we rely on the consent and for [[LEGAL: Q14 retention period for consent evidence, usually at least the statute of limitations, for example 4 to 5 years]] after.\n\n## Privacy\n\nYour mobile number and consent are handled under our Privacy Notice. **No mobile information will be shared with third parties or affiliates for marketing or promotional purposes.** Text-messaging originator opt-in data and consent are not shared with any third party, other than the service providers that deliver messages for us.\n\n## Push notifications\n\nPush notifications go to your phone from our apps. You control them in your device settings and in Your account > Notifications. Push notifications can show on a locked screen; turn them off if you don''t want that.\n\n## Email\n\nEvery marketing email has a one-click unsubscribe link. Emails about orders, bookings, payments, help requests, store credit, membership billing and security are not marketing and cannot be turned off while your account is open.\n\n## Changes\n\nIf we change the program in a way that matters (for example, a new kind of message or a higher frequency), we ask you again before we send. Last updated: see the version and date at the top of this page.\n\n## Contact\n\n{phone} · {privacy} · {address}. Disability or accessibility help: {accessibility}."}'::jsonb, 'Adds WhatsApp with its own opt-in, the exact consent text, consent records, keyword list and quiet hours, and separates account messages from marketing messages.', now(), 'legal-loader', now(), null
 where not exists (select 1 from legal_version where doc_type = 'sms-terms' and (major, minor, patch) >= (1, 0, 0));
update legal_version set effective_date = '2026-12-01'::date, draft_banner = true,
