There is no cancel button yet, so this is done by our team. [[LEGAL: Q08 confirm the wording]]\n- **After the card is sent,** it cannot be cancelled and the purchase is not refundable, except where the law requires it, or where we decide in a help request that the card was bought in error or by fraud and has not been redeemed.\n- **If the card was bought with a payment that is later disputed or reversed,** we may remove the unspent balance and recover the amount.\n\n## Lost, stolen or wrong email\n\nTreat a gift card code like cash. We are not responsible for a card that is lost, stolen, sent to the wrong address or used by someone else after you share the code. If you think that a code was sent to the wrong person, or was stolen, tell us at once through Your account > Get help with an order or {phone}. If the card has not been redeemed, we may be able to cancel it and issue a new one after we check your identity and the purchase, which we do at our discretion. If it has been redeemed, the credit is in someone''s account and we cannot take it back unless it was obtained by fraud.\n\n## Fraud and scams\n\nAfroTransact will never ask you to pay by gift card, to read out a gift card code over the phone or chat, or to buy gift cards for an agency or a prize. If someone asks you to, it is a scam. Tell us. We may freeze or cancel a card, or the credit it became, that we believe is linked to fraud, a scam, money laundering, sanctions, a stolen payment method or a breach of our terms, and we may report it to the authorities.\n\n## Using gift card credit\n\nCredit from a gift card can be used for products and services on AfroTransact, subject to the Store Credit Terms. It can pay for all or part of an order; the rest is paid by card. Refunds go back to whoever paid, the way they paid; credit paid is returned as credit. Credit cannot be used to buy gift cards. [[LEGAL: Q08 confirm]]\n\n## Unclaimed property\n\nSome states have unclaimed property (escheat) laws that may apply to unused gift cards or credit. We follow the law that applies. We may need to hold or report details of unredeemed gift cards or unused balances, and we may contact you before we do. [[LEGAL: Q08 which states exempt gift cards from escheat, and what to say about balances that we might have to report]]\n\n## Our right to change these terms\n\nWe can change these terms for gift cards bought in the future. A change will not reduce the value of a card you already hold. Gift cards are also covered by the Conditions of Use.\n\n## Contact\n\nHelp: Your account > Get help with an order. Phone: {phone}. Email: {legal}. Address: {address}."}'::jsonb, change_summary = 'New. First terms for AfroTransact gift cards, bought with a normal payment and redeemed into the recipient''s store credit.', created_at = now(), updated_at = now()
    where doc_type = 'gift-card-terms' and (major, minor, patch) = (1, 0, 0) and status = 'CURRENT'
      and created_by in ('seed', 'legal-loader') and updated_at = created_at;

