select '2378cc76-2d35-585d-8165-063852726ee5'::uuid, 'store-credit-terms', '1.0', 1, 0, 0, '2026-12-01'::date, 'CURRENT', true,
       '{"en": "# Store Credit Terms\n\n## What store credit is\n\nStore credit is a balance in US dollars (USD) on your AfroTransact account. You can use it to pay for products and services on AfroTransact. It is kept as a running record (a ledger) of every addition and every use, so your balance is always the total of that record, and you can see the record in Your account > AfroTransact credit.\n\nStore credit is issued by [[LEGAL: Q01 legal entity name]] (\"AfroTransact\", \"we\"). It is not money in a bank account. It is not a deposit, does not earn interest, is not insured by the FDIC or any government agency, and is not a payment instrument or a prepaid card. [[LEGAL: Q12 confirm the characterisation and whether any state stored-value, money-transmitter or prepaid access rule applies to closed-loop credit]]\n\n## How you can get store credit\n\n- **Refunds.** When part of an order you paid for with credit is refunded, that part returns as credit. See the Returns, Refunds and Problems With Your Order page.\n- **Gift cards.** The value of a gift card you redeem becomes credit. See the Gift Card Terms.\n- **Referral rewards.** Rewards from the referral program are paid as credit. See the Referral Program Terms.\n- **Plus membership.** Some membership benefits, such as credit back on delivered orders or a monthly credit, are paid as credit. See the Plus Membership Terms.\n- **Decisions by our team.** Our team may add credit to settle a help request or as a goodwill gesture. A record of why is kept. In a help decision, our team may also send the card part of a refund to credit instead of to the card; only our team can do this, with a reason, and it is one way (see the Returns page).\n\n## What you can do with it\n\nYou can use credit to buy products and services on AfroTransact, subject to these terms. At checkout, you choose whether to apply your credit; if the credit is less than the total, the rest is charged to your card or another payment method. [[LEGAL: Q12 confirm whether credit is applied by default or only when selected, and whether it can pay for gift cards, membership fees, delivery fees, taxes and services deposits]]\n\nCredit is used atomically: if your order is placed, the credit is spent once and only once. If the order is cancelled before it ships, the credit comes back to your balance at once.\n\n## What you can never do with it\n\n**Store credit can never be converted to cash.** There is no cash-out, no payout, no refund of credit to a card or a bank account, and no way to transfer credit to another person, account or business. This is how the product works, and our staff have no option to change it.\n\nCredit cannot be sold, bought, traded, pledged or exchanged, and it cannot be used for anything other than products and services on AfroTransact. [[LEGAL: Q08 and Q12 where state law requires cash back on small balances of gift cards or credit, we will follow it; counsel to list those states]]\n\n## Refunds and credit\n\nRefunds always go back to whoever paid, the way they paid. When you paid for an order part with credit and part with a card, the credit part returns as credit and the card part returns to the card. Customers cannot ask for the card part to come back as credit. Customers also cannot ask for credit to come back as card money. See the Returns page.\n\nIf credit was given for something that is later refunded, cancelled or reversed (for example credit back on an order that you then get refunded, or a referral reward for an order that is refunded), we may take back that credit. If you have already spent it, we may reduce credit you later receive, or we may ask you to pay the difference. [[LEGAL: Q12 whether negative balances and clawbacks are acceptable under the law and whether to cap them]]\n\n## Expiry and fees\n\nStore credit does not expire and we do not charge fees for holding it, unless the law allows or requires otherwise. Certain promotional credit may have an end date, which we will show where it is given and before you accept it. [[LEGAL: Q08 and Q12 confirm. Promotional credit with an end date is a business option, not a product requirement; remove this sentence unless the business wants it]]\n\n## Staff adjustments\n\nOur team can add credit, and can correct or remove credit, for example to fix a mistake, to reverse a fraud or a payment dispute, or to carry out a legal duty. Each adjustment has a reason and is recorded with who made it. Larger adjustments need a second approval. You can ask us to explain any entry in your credit record.\n\n## Fraud and misuse\n\nWe may freeze, reduce or cancel credit that we reasonably believe was obtained or used by fraud, abuse, a stolen or disputed payment, a breach of the Conditions of Use or the program terms (for example a referral abuse), or that is linked to a scam. We may also limit how much credit can be used in one order. We may close an account that does so, and we will tell you as the law requires.\n\n## If you close your account\n\nBefore we close your account at your request, we will remind you of any credit. Credit cannot be turned into cash when the account closes. After an account closes, any remaining credit is lost, unless the law requires otherwise or we agree to restore it if you reopen the account within [[LEGAL: Q12 period during which credit is preserved after closure, for example 90 days]]. If we close your account for a reason other than a breach of our terms, we will give you a reasonable time to use your credit first.\n\n## Deceased account holders\n\nIf an account holder dies, a representative may contact us at {legal}. Credit cannot be paid out in cash; we will discuss what we can do in line with the law. [[LEGAL: Q12 confirm approach]]\n\n## Unclaimed property\n\nSome state laws on unclaimed property may apply to unused credit. We will follow the law that applies and may need to report or transfer some balances. [[LEGAL: Q08 confirm]]\n\n## Changes\n\nWe can change these terms for credit you receive in the future and will tell you before the change. We will not reduce a balance you already have, except as these terms say.\n\n## Contact\n\nHelp: Your account > Get help with an order. Phone: {phone}. Email: {legal}. Address: {address}."}'::jsonb, 'New. Sets out how AfroTransact store credit is earned, used and ended, and that it can never be converted to cash.', now(), 'legal-loader', now(), null
 where not exists (select 1 from legal_version where doc_type = 'store-credit-terms' and (major, minor, patch) >= (1, 0, 0));
update legal_version set effective_date = '2026-12-01'::date, draft_banner = true,
       bodies = '{"en": "# Store Credit Terms\n\n## What store credit is\n\nStore credit is a balance in US dollars (USD) on your AfroTransact account. You can use it to pay for products and services on AfroTransact. It is kept as a running record (a ledger) of every addition and every use, so your balance is always the total of that record, and you can see the record in Your account > AfroTransact credit.\n\nStore credit is issued by [[LEGAL: Q01 legal entity name]] (\"AfroTransact\", \"we\"). It is not money in a bank account. It is not a deposit, does not earn interest, is not insured by the FDIC or any government agency, and is not a payment instrument or a prepaid card. [[LEGAL: Q12 confirm the characterisation and whether any state stored-value, money-transmitter or prepaid access rule applies to closed-loop credit]]\n\n## How you can get store credit\n\n- **Refunds.** When part of an order you paid for with credit is refunded, that part returns as credit. See the Returns, Refunds and Problems With Your Order page.\n- **Gift cards.** The value of a gift card you redeem becomes credit. See the Gift Card Terms.\n- **Referral rewards.** Rewards from the referral program are paid as credit. See the Referral Program Terms.\n- **Plus membership.** Some membership benefits, such as credit back on delivered orders or a monthly credit, are paid as credit. See the Plus Membership Terms.\n- **Decisions by our team.** Our team may add credit to settle a help request or as a goodwill gesture. A record of why is kept. In a help decision, our team may also send the card part of a refund to credit instead of to the card; only our team can do this, with a reason, and it is one way (see the Returns page).\n\n## What you can do with it\n\nYou can use credit to buy products and services on AfroTransact, subject to these terms. At checkout, you choose whether to apply your credit; if the credit is less than the total, the rest is charged to your card or another payment method. [[LEGAL: Q12 confirm whether credit is applied by default or only when selected, and whether it can pay for gift cards, membership fees, delivery fees, taxes and services deposits]]\n\nCredit is used atomically: if your order is placed, the credit is spent once and only once. If the order is cancelled before it ships, the credit comes back to your balance at once.\n\n## What you can never do with it\n\n**Store credit can never be converted to cash.** There is no cash-out, no payout, no refund of credit to a card or a bank account, and no way to transfer credit to another person, account or business. This is how the product works, and our staff have no option to change it.\n\nCredit cannot be sold, bought, traded, pledged or exchanged, and it cannot be used for anything other than products and services on AfroTransact. [[LEGAL: Q08 and Q12 where state law requires cash back on small balances of gift cards or credit, we will follow it; counsel to list those states]]\n\n## Refunds and credit\n\nRefunds always go back to whoever paid, the way they paid. When you paid for an order part with credit and part with a card, the credit part returns as credit and the card part returns to the card. Customers cannot ask for the card part to come back as credit. Customers also cannot ask for credit to come back as card money. See the Returns page.\n\nIf credit was given for something that is later refunded, cancelled or reversed (for example credit back on an order that you then get refunded, or a referral reward for an order that is refunded), we may take back that credit. If you have already spent it, we may reduce credit you later receive, or we may ask you to pay the difference. [[LEGAL: Q12 whether negative balances and clawbacks are acceptable under the law and whether to cap them]]\n\n## Expiry and fees\n\nStore credit does not expire and we do not charge fees for holding it, unless the law allows or requires otherwise. Certain promotional credit may have an end date, which we will show where it is given and before you accept it. [[LEGAL: Q08 and Q12 confirm. Promotional credit with an end date is a business option, not a product requirement; remove this sentence unless the business wants it]]\n\n## Staff adjustments\n\nOur team can add credit, and can correct or remove credit, for example to fix a mistake, to reverse a fraud or a payment dispute, or to carry out a legal duty. Each adjustment has a reason and is recorded with who made it. Larger adjustments need a second approval. You can ask us to explain any entry in your credit record.\n\n## Fraud and misuse\n\nWe may freeze, reduce or cancel credit that we reasonably believe was obtained or used by fraud, abuse, a stolen or disputed payment, a breach of the Conditions of Use or the program terms (for example a referral abuse), or that is linked to a scam. We may also limit how much credit can be used in one order. We may close an account that does so, and we will tell you as the law requires.\n\n## If you close your account\n\nBefore we close your account at your request, we will remind you of any credit. Credit cannot be turned into cash when the account closes. After an account closes, any remaining credit is lost, unless the law requires otherwise or we agree to restore it if you reopen the account within [[LEGAL: Q12 period during which credit is preserved after closure, for example 90 days]]. If we close your account for a reason other than a breach of our terms, we will give you a reasonable time to use your credit first.\n\n## Deceased account holders\n\nIf an account holder dies, a representative may contact us at {legal}. Credit cannot be paid out in cash; we will discuss what we can do in line with the law. [[LEGAL: Q12 confirm approach]]\n\n## Unclaimed property\n\nSome state laws on unclaimed property may apply to unused credit. We will follow the law that applies and may need to report or transfer some balances. [[LEGAL: Q08 confirm]]\n\n## Changes\n\nWe can change these terms for credit you receive in the future and will tell you before the change. We will not reduce a balance you already have, except as these terms say.\n\n## Contact\n\nHelp: Your account > Get help with an order. Phone: {phone}. Email: {legal}. Address: {address}."}'::jsonb, change_summary = 'New. Sets out how AfroTransact store credit is earned, used and ended, and that it can never be converted to cash.', created_at = now(), updated_at = now()
    where doc_type = 'store-credit-terms' and (major, minor, patch) = (1, 0, 0) and status = 'CURRENT'
      and created_by in ('seed', 'legal-loader') and updated_at = created_at;

-- membership-terms 1.0 (effective 2026-12-01; locales: en; draft banner on)
delete from legal_version where doc_type = 'membership-terms' and created_by = 'seed'
    and exists (select 1 from legal_version c where c.doc_type = 'membership-terms' and c.status = 'CURRENT'
                and c.created_by = 'seed' and c.updated_at = c.created_at and (c.major, c.minor, c.patch) > (1, 0, 0));
update legal_version set status = 'ARCHIVED', archived_at = now(), updated_at = now()
    where doc_type = 'membership-terms' and status = 'CURRENT' and (major, minor, patch) < (1, 0, 0);
insert into legal_version (id, doc_type, version, major, minor, patch, effective_date, status, draft_banner, bodies,
                           change_summary, created_at, created_by, updated_at, archived_at)
select '3a34b4d2-d43f-5222-9f60-984198b5f2a9'::uuid, 'membership-terms', '1.0', 1, 0, 0, '2026-12-01'::date, 'CURRENT', true,
       '{"en": "# Plus Membership Terms\n\n## What this is\n\nAfroTransact offers paid memberships with benefits for shoppers. We call the first one **Plus**. We may offer other tiers (for example a higher one), and we may change which tiers are offered. These terms apply to every tier. The plan name, price, trial length and benefits that apply to you are shown on the sign-up page and in the confirmation email, and in Your account > Membership. If anything in this document is different from what the sign-up page shows for your tier, the sign-up page for your tier wins for price and benefits.\n\nThe membership is provided by [[LEGAL: Q01 legal entity name]] (\"AfroTransact\", \"we\").\n\n## Example of the Plus tier at launch\n\nThe Plus tier at launch is planned to be $9.99 a month or $99 a year (USD), with a 14-day free trial, and free AfroTransact delivery and free carrier shipping on orders of $25 or more. These amounts are examples and can change before launch; the sign-up page shows the exact price, trial and benefits that apply when you join. [[LEGAL: Q09 replace the example with the final launch numbers, or remove the example]]\n\n## Benefits\n\nEach tier has a set of benefits that we choose from a list and that we may change over time. Benefits can include:\n\n- **Free delivery and carrier shipping** on orders over an order minimum, up to a limit per order. Pickup and express options are not covered.\n- **Credit back** on delivered orders, as a percent of what you spend, paid as store credit.\n- **A monthly credit** paid as store credit.\n- **Early access** to pre-order windows and delivery runs.\n- **Priority support.**\n- **Bigger referral or gift rewards.**\n- **Member prices or deals,** where shown on a product.\n\nThe benefits of your tier are shown at sign-up and in Your account > Membership, and each order shows the benefits that were applied. Credit benefits start with your first paid period and not during a free trial. Store credit from a membership follows the Store Credit Terms, so it can never be converted to cash. If a benefit is changed or removed, we will give you notice, and you can cancel. The changes do not affect benefits already earned on orders already placed.\n\n## Free trial\n\nIf your tier has a trial, the sign-up page tells you how long it is and what you will pay when it ends. A trial is available once per customer and once per card. If you started a membership before, or you use a card that has already been used for a trial, you are not eligible, and you will be told that you will be charged for the first period when you join. **Unless you cancel before the trial ends, your membership continues and we will charge your payment method the price of the first period.** We will remind you before the trial ends (see \"Reminders\").\n\n## Automatic renewal: what you agree to\n\n**Please read this section.** When you join, you agree that:\n\n1. Your membership **renews automatically** at the end of each period (each month for a monthly plan, each year for a yearly plan) **until you cancel**.\n2. We will **charge the payment method you chose** (or the one you later set as your default for the membership) for the price shown **at the start of each period**, plus any tax that applies, using the card authorisation you give us at sign-up. This is a recurring charge. You authorise us and Stripe to make it without asking you again each time.\n3. The price is the price shown to you at sign-up. We lock it for your membership. If we want to change the price for existing members, we will tell you in advance, by email, at least [[LEGAL: Q09 notice period for price changes; some state laws require a specific period, for example 7 to 30 days]] days before the change and before the next charge, and you can cancel before it takes effect.\n4. You can **cancel at any time** (see \"How to cancel\"). We will not charge you again after you cancel.\n\nYou give your express consent to these terms by ticking the unticked consent box (or by the equivalent clear action) and pressing the button on the sign-up page, which shows the price, how often you will be charged, the length of the trial, that the membership renews until you cancel, and how to cancel, next to the button, before you pay. We send you a confirmation by email after you sign up, with these terms and instructions on how to cancel. We keep a record of what you agreed to, when, and which version of these terms.\n\n[[LEGAL: Q09 counsel to confirm that the sign-up page, confirmation email, reminders and cancellation flow satisfy the federal Restore Online Shoppers'' Confidence Act, the FTC Act, the FTC''s negative-option rule if it is in force when we launch, and the automatic renewal laws of California, Colorado, Illinois, New York, Virginia and every other state in which we launch, including disclosure placement, consent record keeping and online cancellation requirements]]\n\n## How to cancel\n\nYou can cancel **online, any time, in the same way you signed up**: go to Your account > Membership and choose **Cancel membership**. You can also cancel from the confirmation email link, in the mobile app, or by contacting support at {phone} or through Your account > Get help with an order. You do not have to call, chat with an agent, give a reason, or go through special offers to cancel. After you cancel, we show a confirmation on screen and by email.\n\nWhen you cancel:\n\n- No further renewal charge is made.\n- Your benefits **continue until the end of the period you already paid for**, unless you take the refund described below, in which case they end at once.\n- If you cancel during a trial, you will not be charged and the membership ends at the end of the trial, unless you ask for it to end at once.\n- You can **resume** the membership at any time before the end of the period, and the cancellation is undone. After it ends, you can join again.\n\n## Refunds\n\nIf you cancel **within [[LEGAL: Q09 refund window, currently 7 days by platform default]] days after a charge, and before you have used any benefit** of that period (for example before a free delivery waiver was applied to an order, or before credit was paid), you can ask for the whole membership fee back to the card you paid with, and your membership ends at once. The membership page shows whether you qualify and why not if you do not (for example, the window has passed or a benefit was used). Otherwise, the fee is not refundable and your benefits continue to the end of the period. Our team can refund a fee in other cases with a reason, such as when we charged you by mistake. Store credit already paid to you as a membership benefit is not paid out in cash; if you take a refund, the credit-back from that period may be taken back.\n\nWhere the law gives you a right to a refund, that right applies.\n\n## Failed payments\n\nIf a renewal payment fails, your membership shows as past due. We try again on the days we set (by default, after 1, 3 and 5 days). Your benefits stay on while we retry. We will email you each time and ask you to update your payment method. If the last try fails, the membership ends (lapses) and the benefits stop. You can join again at any time. You are not charged for a period where the payment failed.\n\n## Changing your plan\n\n- **Upgrading** to a higher tier or a longer interval takes effect straight away. We charge the difference for the unused part of the current period.\n- **Downgrading,** or changing from yearly to monthly, takes effect at the end of the current period.\n- You can take back a scheduled change before it takes effect.\n\n## Reminders\n\nWe send you these notices by email and in the app (and by SMS or push if you chose those):\n\n- A confirmation when you sign up, with the price, trial, renewal terms and how to cancel.\n- A reminder before a trial ends and before the first charge. [[LEGAL: Q09 timing, for example 3 to 7 days before]]\n- A reminder before a **yearly** renewal [[LEGAL: Q09 timing required by state law, for example 15 to 45 days before]], and a notice of a price change or a material change in terms.\n- A receipt after each charge.\n\n## Complimentary membership\n\nSometimes we give free days of membership, for example as a referral reward or in a promotion. A free membership has an end date and does not need a card. It ends on that date and does not renew into a paid membership unless you choose to join. If you are already a member, free days are added to your current period.\n\n## Taxes\n\nMembership fees are shown before tax. We add sales tax where the law requires it. [[LEGAL: Q20 confirm whether membership fees are taxable in the launch states]]\n\n## Using your membership fairly\n\nMembership is for personal and household use. We can end a membership or take back benefits if we reasonably find abuse, such as repeated returns of a delivery benefit, creating accounts or cards to get more free trials, or reselling goods. We will tell you why, and we will refund the unused part of the current period if we end a membership for a reason other than your breach. See the Conditions of Use.\n\n## Payments by Stripe\n\nMembership fees are processed by Stripe on a card or bank account you saved. By saving the card you agree to Stripe''s terms and acknowledge its privacy policy. You can change the payment method for your membership in Your account > Payment methods.\n\n## Changes to these terms\n\nWe will tell you at least 30 days before a material change to these terms or to your tier, and you can cancel before it takes effect. A change never reduces a period that you have already paid for.\n\n## Contact\n\nHelp: Your account > Get help with an order. Phone: {phone}. Email: {legal}. Address: {address}."}'::jsonb, 'New. Terms for AfroTransact membership tiers (Plus is the example), including automatic renewal disclosures, free trial, cancellation and refund rules.', now(), 'legal-loader', now(), null
 where not exists (select 1 from legal_version where doc_type = 'membership-terms' and (major, minor, patch) >= (1, 0, 0));
update legal_version set effective_date = '2026-12-01'::date, draft_banner = true,
