mbership follows the Store Credit Terms, so it can never be converted to cash. If a benefit is changed or removed, we will give you notice, and you can cancel. The changes do not affect benefits already earned on orders already placed.\n\n## Free trial\n\nIf your tier has a trial, the sign-up page tells you how long it is and what you will pay when it ends. A trial is available once per customer and once per card. If you started a membership before, or you use a card that has already been used for a trial, you are not eligible, and you will be told that you will be charged for the first period when you join. **Unless you cancel before the trial ends, your membership continues and we will charge your payment method the price of the first period.** We will remind you before the trial ends (see \"Reminders\").\n\n## Automatic renewal: what you agree to\n\n**Please read this section.** When you join, you agree that:\n\n1. Your membership **renews automatically** at the end of each period (each month for a monthly plan, each year for a yearly plan) **until you cancel**.\n2. We will **charge the payment method you chose** (or the one you later set as your default for the membership) for the price shown **at the start of each period**, plus any tax that applies, using the card authorisation you give us at sign-up. This is a recurring charge. You authorise us and Stripe to make it without asking you again each time.\n3. The price is the price shown to you at sign-up. We lock it for your membership. If we want to change the price for existing members, we will tell you in advance, by email, at least [[LEGAL: Q09 notice period for price changes; some state laws require a specific period, for example 7 to 30 days]] days before the change and before the next charge, and you can cancel before it takes effect.\n4. You can **cancel at any time** (see \"How to cancel\"). We will not charge you again after you cancel.\n\nYou give your express consent to these terms by ticking the unticked consent box (or by the equivalent clear action) and pressing the button on the sign-up page, which shows the price, how often you will be charged, the length of the trial, that the membership renews until you cancel, and how to cancel, next to the button, before you pay. We send you a confirmation by email after you sign up, with these terms and instructions on how to cancel. We keep a record of what you agreed to, when, and which version of these terms.\n\n[[LEGAL: Q09 counsel to confirm that the sign-up page, confirmation email, reminders and cancellation flow satisfy the federal Restore Online Shoppers'' Confidence Act, the FTC Act, the FTC''s negative-option rule if it is in force when we launch, and the automatic renewal laws of California, Colorado, Illinois, New York, Virginia and every other state in which we launch, including disclosure placement, consent record keeping and online cancellation requirements]]\n\n## How to cancel\n\nYou can cancel **online, any time, in the same way you signed up**: go to Your account > Membership and choose **Cancel membership**. You can also cancel from the confirmation email link, in the mobile app, or by contacting support at {phone} or through Your account > Get help with an order. You do not have to call, chat with an agent, give a reason, or go through special offers to cancel. After you cancel, we show a confirmation on screen and by email.\n\nWhen you cancel:\n\n- No further renewal charge is made.\n- Your benefits **continue until the end of the period you already paid for**, unless you take the refund described below, in which case they end at once.\n- If you cancel during a trial, you will not be charged and the membership ends at the end of the trial, unless you ask for it to end at once.\n- You can **resume** the membership at any time before the end of the period, and the cancellation is undone. After it ends, you can join again.\n\n## Refunds\n\nIf you cancel **within [[LEGAL: Q09 refund window, currently 7 days by platform default]] days after a charge, and before you have used any benefit** of that period (for example before a free delivery waiver was applied to an order, or before credit was paid), you can ask for the whole membership fee back to the card you paid with, and your membership ends at once. The membership page shows whether you qualify and why not if you do not (for example, the window has passed or a benefit was used). Otherwise, the fee is not refundable and your benefits continue to the end of the period. Our team can refund a fee in other cases with a reason, such as when we charged you by mistake. Store credit already paid to you as a membership benefit is not paid out in cash; if you take a refund, the credit-back from that period may be taken back.\n\nWhere the law gives you a right to a refund, that right applies.\n\n## Failed payments\n\nIf a renewal payment fails, your membership shows as past due. We try again on the days we set (by default, after 1, 3 and 5 days). Your benefits stay on while we retry. We will email you each time and ask you to update your payment method. If the last try fails, the membership ends (lapses) and the benefits stop. You can join again at any time. You are not charged for a period where the payment failed.\n\n## Changing your plan\n\n- **Upgrading** to a higher tier or a longer interval takes effect straight away. We charge the difference for the unused part of the current period.\n- **Downgrading,** or changing from yearly to monthly, takes effect at the end of the current period.\n- You can take back a scheduled change before it takes effect.\n\n## Reminders\n\nWe send you these notices by email and in the app (and by SMS or push if you chose those):\n\n- A confirmation when you sign up, with the price, trial, renewal terms and how to cancel.\n- A reminder before a trial ends and before the first charge. [[LEGAL: Q09 timing, for example 3 to 7 days before]]\n- A reminder before a **yearly** renewal [[LEGAL: Q09 timing required by state law, for example 15 to 45 days before]], and a notice of a price change or a material change in terms.\n- A receipt after each charge.\n\n## Complimentary membership\n\nSometimes we give free days of membership, for example as a referral reward or in a promotion. A free membership has an end date and does not need a card. It ends on that date and does not renew into a paid membership unless you choose to join. If you are already a member, free days are added to your current period.\n\n## Taxes\n\nMembership fees are shown before tax. We add sales tax where the law requires it. [[LEGAL: Q20 confirm whether membership fees are taxable in the launch states]]\n\n## Using your membership fairly\n\nMembership is for personal and household use. We can end a membership or take back benefits if we reasonably find abuse, such as repeated returns of a delivery benefit, creating accounts or cards to get more free trials, or reselling goods. We will tell you why, and we will refund the unused part of the current period if we end a membership for a reason other than your breach. See the Conditions of Use.\n\n## Payments by Stripe\n\nMembership fees are processed by Stripe on a card or bank account you saved. By saving the card you agree to Stripe''s terms and acknowledge its privacy policy. You can change the payment method for your membership in Your account > Payment methods.\n\n## Changes to these terms\n\nWe will tell you at least 30 days before a material change to these terms or to your tier, and you can cancel before it takes effect. A change never reduces a period that you have already paid for.\n\n## Contact\n\nHelp: Your account > Get help with an order. Phone: {phone}. Email: {legal}. Address: {address}."}'::jsonb, change_summary = 'New. Terms for AfroTransact membership tiers (Plus is the example), including automatic renewal disclosures, free trial, cancellation and refund rules.', created_at = now(), updated_at = now()
    where doc_type = 'membership-terms' and (major, minor, patch) = (1, 0, 0) and status = 'CURRENT'
      and created_by in ('seed', 'legal-loader') and updated_at = created_at;

-- referral-terms 1.0 (effective 2026-12-01; locales: en; draft banner on)
delete from legal_version where doc_type = 'referral-terms' and created_by = 'seed'
    and exists (select 1 from legal_version c where c.doc_type = 'referral-terms' and c.status = 'CURRENT'
                and c.created_by = 'seed' and c.updated_at = c.created_at and (c.major, c.minor, c.patch) > (1, 0, 0));
update legal_version set status = 'ARCHIVED', archived_at = now(), updated_at = now()
    where doc_type = 'referral-terms' and status = 'CURRENT' and (major, minor, patch) < (1, 0, 0);
insert into legal_version (id, doc_type, version, major, minor, patch, effective_date, status, draft_banner, bodies,
                           change_summary, created_at, created_by, updated_at, archived_at)
select 'd3ff934e-5589-5aa5-a820-ab5a6156becf'::uuid, 'referral-terms', '1.0', 1, 0, 0, '2026-12-01'::date, 'CURRENT', true,
       '{"en": "# Referral Program Terms\n\n## How the program works\n\nThe referral program is run and paid for by AfroTransact ([[LEGAL: Q01 legal entity name]], \"we\"). It is not run by sellers or providers. When you share your referral code or link and a friend signs up with it and then makes a qualifying order, we reward you both.\n\nThe amounts, rules and dates below are examples. We set the real ones in the program settings, and the app shows the current reward for you and for your friend, and the conditions, before you share and before your friend signs up. If something here is different from what the app shows, the app shows what applies.\n\n## Example of the rewards\n\nAt launch we plan this reward: **$10 in store credit for you and $10 in store credit for your friend,** after your friend''s **first order of at least $30 has been delivered and its problem-reporting period has passed** (the \"return window\", which is **30 days** after delivery by default). [[LEGAL: Q24 replace the example with the final launch numbers and period]]\n\nA reward can instead be a number of days of free membership, or a different amount, and it can be different for the person who refers and the person who is referred. The program may also have limits (see \"Limits\").\n\n## Who can take part\n\n- You must have an AfroTransact account in good standing and be 18 or older.\n- Your friend must be a **new customer** who has never had an AfroTransact account, and who signs up using your code or link. A code typed after sign-up cannot be added later. [[LEGAL: Q24 confirm]]\n- You cannot refer yourself, someone in your household, or an account you control. Staff accounts and business accounts are not eligible. [[LEGAL: Q24 confirm]]\n\n## When a reward is earned\n\nA reward is earned only when **all** the following are true:\n\n1. Your friend signed up with your code or link, within the time limit the app shows (by default 90 days from sign-up to qualify).\n2. Your friend placed an order that meets the minimum order value, and that order was **delivered**. Only the value of goods that stayed delivered counts. If the order is refunded so that it falls below the minimum, it does not qualify.\n3. The problem-reporting (return) window for that order has passed without it being refunded below the minimum.\n4. The program is on, you and your friend have passed our checks, and neither of you is breaking these terms.\n\nWhere a delivery or refund is still being reviewed, the reward waits. If a smaller first order does not reach the minimum, a later delivered order can still qualify within the time limit. You can see a referral that is waiting in Your account > Refer a friend.\n\n## How rewards are paid\n\nRewards are paid as **store credit** (or, if the app says so, free days of membership). They follow the Store Credit Terms, so credit can only be used to buy products and services and can never be converted to cash, and cannot be transferred. A reward is not income paid for a service, and it is not for sale. [[LEGAL: Q24 confirm tax treatment, and whether reporting is needed for high-value referrers]] A reward paid to a Plus member may be larger if the member''s tier gives bigger rewards.\n\n## Limits\n\nWe may limit how many rewarded referrals one person can have and how much referral credit they can earn in total. By default, the limits are 20 rewarded referrals and $500 of referral credit per person. The limits apply to each side on its own, so your limit does not stop your friend from being rewarded. The app shows the current limits. [[LEGAL: Q24 confirm]]\n\n## Abuse rules and checks\n\nDo not abuse the program. You may not: create fake or duplicate accounts; refer yourself or people in your household; use a friend''s payment method, address or device to pass the checks; post your code on coupon, deal or paid-advertising sites in a way that suggests that it is a public discount; send spam or unwanted messages; use misleading claims about AfroTransact or the reward; pay or trade for referrals; or place orders only to collect the reward and then cause them to be refunded.\n\nTo find abuse, we compare technical signals from sign-up and ordering: the sign-up device and network, the delivery address and the saved payment card (stored in a one-way form, not in the clear). The same device, network, address or card on both the referrer and the friend is a sign that two accounts belong to the **same household or person**. **We allow one referral reward per household.** [[LEGAL: Q24 and Q11 confirm the privacy wording and how to describe a household]] Referrals that look suspicious are held for review by our team. You will see a held referral as \"waiting\" and not the reason.\n\n## Our rights\n\nWe may **withhold, reduce, delay or cancel** a reward, and take back credit already paid, if we reasonably believe the rules were broken, a payment was reversed or an order was refunded or cancelled, or the referral came from abuse. We may suspend or end an account involved in abuse. We decide if a referral qualifies; our decision will be explained if you ask. We can change, pause or end the program at any time; **changes apply to future referrals**, and a reward already earned is honoured. If the program is switched off, referrals pause and resume when it is back on, within the time limits.\n\n## Your friend''s privacy\n\nWhen you refer a friend, you see only whether the referral is pending or rewarded; you never see their orders, name or address. Your friend sees that they joined with a code. Please only share your code with people who want to hear from you. Do not send messages that break the law, including the rules on commercial texts and email: your friend must have agreed to hear from you. We do not send marketing texts to your friend because of your referral unless they opt in to them.\n\n## Promotional claims\n\nIf you tell others about AfroTransact online and you are rewarded, you must say clearly that you get a reward for referrals, as the FTC''s endorsement rules require. [[LEGAL: Q24 confirm disclosure wording and whether program is a promotion subject to state registration]]\n\n## Changes\n\nWe may change these terms. Material changes will be notified before they take effect. See the Conditions of Use.\n\n## Contact\n\nHelp: Your account > Get help with an order. Phone: {phone}. Email: {legal}. Address: {address}."}'::jsonb, 'New. Rules for AfroTransact''s refer-a-friend program, rewards paid as store credit or membership days, and abuse checks.', now(), 'legal-loader', now(), null
 where not exists (select 1 from legal_version where doc_type = 'referral-terms' and (major, minor, patch) >= (1, 0, 0));
update legal_version set effective_date = '2026-12-01'::date, draft_banner = true,
       bodies = '{"en": "# Referral Program Terms\n\n## How the program works\n\nThe referral program is run and paid for by AfroTransact ([[LEGAL: Q01 legal entity name]], \"we\"). It is not run by sellers or providers. When you share your referral code or link and a friend signs up with it and then makes a qualifying order, we reward you both.\n\nThe amounts, rules and dates below are examples. We set the real ones in the program settings, and the app shows the current reward for you and for your friend, and the conditions, before you share and before your friend signs up. If something here is different from what the app shows, the app shows what applies.\n\n## Example of the rewards\n\nAt launch we plan this reward: **$10 in store credit for you and $10 in store credit for your friend,** after your friend''s **first order of at least $30 has been delivered and its problem-reporting period has passed** (the \"return window\", which is **30 days** after delivery by default). [[LEGAL: Q24 replace the example with the final launch numbers and period]]\n\nA reward can instead be a number of days of free membership, or a different amount, and it can be different for the person who refers and the person who is referred. The program may also have limits (see \"Limits\").\n\n## Who can take part\n\n- You must have an AfroTransact account in good standing and be 18 or older.\n- Your friend must be a **new customer** who has never had an AfroTransact account, and who signs up using your code or link. A code typed after sign-up cannot be added later. [[LEGAL: Q24 confirm]]\n- You cannot refer yourself, someone in your household, or an account you control. Staff accounts and business accounts are not eligible. [[LEGAL: Q24 confirm]]\n\n## When a reward is earned\n\nA reward is earned only when **all** the following are true:\n\n1. Your friend signed up with your code or link, within the time limit the app shows (by default 90 days from sign-up to qualify).\n2. Your friend placed an order that meets the minimum order value, and that order was **delivered**. Only the value of goods that stayed delivered counts. If the order is refunded so that it falls below the minimum, it does not qualify.\n3. The problem-reporting (return) window for that order has passed without it being refunded below the minimum.\n4. The program is on, you and your friend have passed our checks, and neither of you is breaking these terms.\n\nWhere a delivery or refund is still being reviewed, the reward waits. If a smaller first order does not reach the minimum, a later delivered order can still qualify within the time limit. You can see a referral that is waiting in Your account > Refer a friend.\n\n## How rewards are paid\n\nRewards are paid as **store credit** (or, if the app says so, free days of membership). They follow the Store Credit Terms, so credit can only be used to buy products and services and can never be converted to cash, and cannot be transferred. A reward is not income paid for a service, and it is not for sale. [[LEGAL: Q24 confirm tax treatment, and whether reporting is needed for high-value referrers]] A reward paid to a Plus member may be larger if the member''s tier gives bigger rewards.\n\n## Limits\n\nWe may limit how many rewarded referrals one person can have and how much referral credit they can earn in total. By default, the limits are 20 rewarded referrals and $500 of referral credit per person. The limits apply to each side on its own, so your limit does not stop your friend from being rewarded. The app shows the current limits. [[LEGAL: Q24 confirm]]\n\n## Abuse rules and checks\n\nDo not abuse the program. You may not: create fake or duplicate accounts; refer yourself or people in your household; use a friend''s payment method, address or device to pass the checks; post your code on coupon, deal or paid-advertising sites in a way that suggests that it is a public discount; send spam or unwanted messages; use misleading claims about AfroTransact or the reward; pay or trade for referrals; or place orders only to collect the reward and then cause them to be refunded.\n\nTo find abuse, we compare technical signals from sign-up and ordering: the sign-up device and network, the delivery address and the saved payment card (stored in a one-way form, not in the clear). The same device, network, address or card on both the referrer and the friend is a sign that two accounts belong to the **same household or person**. **We allow one referral reward per household.** [[LEGAL: Q24 and Q11 confirm the privacy wording and how to describe a household]] Referrals that look suspicious are held for review by our team. You will see a held referral as \"waiting\" and not the reason.\n\n## Our rights\n\nWe may **withhold, reduce, delay or cancel** a reward, and take back credit already paid, if we reasonably believe the rules were broken, a payment was reversed or an order was refunded or cancelled, or the referral came from abuse. We may suspend or end an account involved in abuse. We decide if a referral qualifies; our decision will be explained if you ask. We can change, pause or end the program at any time; **changes apply to future referrals**, and a reward already earned is honoured. If the program is switched off, referrals pause and resume when it is back on, within the time limits.\n\n## Your friend''s privacy\n\nWhen you refer a friend, you see only whether the referral is pending or rewarded; you never see their orders, name or address. Your friend sees that they joined with a code. Please only share your code with people who want to hear from you. Do not send messages that break the law, including the rules on commercial texts and email: your friend must have agreed to hear from you. We do not send marketing texts to your friend because of your referral unless they opt in to them.\n\n## Promotional claims\n\nIf you tell others about AfroTransact online and you are rewarded, you must say clearly that you get a reward for referrals, as the FTC''s endorsement rules require. [[LEGAL: Q24 confirm disclosure wording and whether program is a promotion subject to state registration]]\n\n## Changes\n\nWe may change these terms. Material changes will be notified before they take effect. See the Conditions of Use.\n\n## Contact\n\nHelp: Your account > Get help with an order. Phone: {phone}. Email: {legal}. Address: {address}."}'::jsonb, change_summary = 'New. Rules for AfroTransact''s refer-a-friend program, rewards paid as store credit or membership days, and abuse checks.', created_at = now(), updated_at = now()
    where doc_type = 'referral-terms' and (major, minor, patch) = (1, 0, 0) and status = 'CURRENT'
      and created_by in ('seed', 'legal-loader') and updated_at = created_at;

-- preorder-delivery-terms 1.0 (effective 2026-12-01; locales: en; draft banner on)
delete from legal_version where doc_type = 'preorder-delivery-terms' and created_by = 'seed'
    and exists (select 1 from legal_version c where c.doc_type = 'preorder-delivery-terms' and c.status = 'CURRENT'
                and c.created_by = 'seed' and c.updated_at = c.created_at and (c.major, c.minor, c.patch) > (1, 0, 0));
update legal_version set status = 'ARCHIVED', archived_at = now(), updated_at = now()
    where doc_type = 'preorder-delivery-terms' and status = 'CURRENT' and (major, minor, patch) < (1, 0, 0);
insert into legal_version (id, doc_type, version, major, minor, patch, effective_date, status, draft_banner, bodies,
