select '1c471544-278c-51e0-a239-e873e37393bc'::uuid, 'preorder-delivery-terms', '1.0', 1, 0, 0, '2026-12-01'::date, 'CURRENT', true,
       '{"en": "# Pre-order and Delivery Run Terms\n\n## What these are\n\nDelivery is expensive when it is one small order to a far place. To keep it fair, we group the orders of one area into one trip. There are two related offers.\n\n- **Pre-order window.** A time window in which you can order products for a set delivery date. When the window closes, the paid orders are delivered, often on a delivery run.\n- **Delivery run.** One planned trip by AfroTransact drivers that brings the orders of one area to their addresses or to pickup points, on a set date. A run is offered only for goods that are already in stock, and only in the places we have switched on.\n\nBoth are ordinary orders with a scheduled delivery. All the Conditions of Use and the Returns, Refunds and Problems With Your Order page apply to them, with the additions below. The offer you see at checkout shows the delivery date, the order cutoff, the fee and how many orders have been placed so far.\n\n## Places we serve\n\nWe start in the US states and cities we have switched on. We offer a run or a window only where the address is inside a covered location. If your address is outside it, we ship by carrier instead, or tell you the order cannot be delivered. Where we serve changes over time. [[LEGAL: Q21 confirm the list of launch states and cities for publication]]\n\n## How you pay\n\nYou are charged like for any other order. At checkout, your card or payment method is authorised for the full amount. We collect the payment for each package when it leaves for you. If a package is cancelled before it leaves, the authorisation is released, so you are not charged; if the money was already collected, it is refunded. Pre-orders and delivery runs never ask for a second payment, and nothing is held back to be charged later. If your payment fails, we release your place in the run. Sales tax and any fee are shown before you place the order. See \"Prices, payment and taxes\" in the Conditions of Use for payment processing by Stripe.\n\n## Order cutoff\n\nEach window and run has a cutoff time. An order placed after the cutoff cannot join it. We show the next open run or window, and if none is open, we say so. An order placed just as the cutoff passes may be refused before you are charged.\n\n## Minimum number of orders\n\nEach window or run has a **minimum number of orders** that we set. We show it at checkout with honest progress, for example \"7 of 10 orders so far\", and we tell you that a run that does not reach its minimum may be cancelled and that you would be refunded in full.\n\n- **If the minimum is reached,** the window or run goes ahead. It may close early once the minimum is reached.\n- **If the end date passes without the minimum,** we make a decision: **cancel** (everyone is refunded) or **proceed** (the orders go ahead as planned). Our team decides, records who decided and why, and tells the customers. Proceeding may mean the delivery date moves, and we tell you if it does.\n- **You can cancel** your own order until its shipment has been prepared, as described in the Returns page.\n\n## If we cancel\n\nIf we cancel a pre-order window or a delivery run, **every order on it is refunded in full, including the delivery fee,** automatically, and the stock is released. If your card was only authorised, the authorisation is released instead, so you are whole either way. You do not have to ask. You will be told by the channels you chose (email, push, and SMS or WhatsApp if you opted in). Refunds appear on your statement according to your bank''s timing. If you paid some of the order with store credit, that part returns as store credit. If only one package of a multi-package order is cancelled, the others are not changed.\n\n## Delivery fees\n\nThe delivery fee depends on the delivery method. The rule that applies to you is shown at checkout, and the amount is recorded on your order. A later change in our fees never changes an order you already placed.\n\n| Method | How the fee is set |\n|---|---|\n| **AfroTransact delivery** (our drivers) | A flat fee set by distance band from the run''s location to your address. Addresses beyond the last band are shipped by carrier instead. |\n| **Carrier shipping** (UPS, USPS, FedEx, DHL Express and others) | The carrier''s rate for the order, or our handling or fallback fee. Some orders over a set value ship free. |\n| **Pickup** (a pickup point, or pickup from the seller) | A pickup fee, which is often zero. |\n\nA window or run can have its own door or pickup fee. A Plus membership can waive the delivery or shipping fee on orders over its minimum (see the Plus Membership Terms). Express options and pickup are not waived. Sales tax may apply to fees where the law says so. [[LEGAL: Q20 confirm]] Fee rules are set by us in our settings and can change; they are never hidden.\n\n## Delivery dates and windows\n\nThe delivery date is our plan, and the delivery window (for example, morning or afternoon) is our best estimate. We do not promise a time. Weather, traffic, vehicle problems, a closed road, safety, the seller''s stock or events outside our control may move a date. We tell you as soon as we can by your notification channels, and if the new date does not work, you can cancel the shipment if it has not been prepared. If we cannot deliver within a reasonable time after the date we gave, contact us through Your account > Get help with an order. [[LEGAL: Q30 confirm delay-notice and cancel-and-refund rules for pre-paid orders under the FTC Mail, Internet or Telephone Order Merchandise Rule and state law]]\n\n## Delivery codes and proof of delivery\n\nEach order that we deliver or that you collect has a **delivery code** (handover code) in your order page and your messages. **Give the code to the driver or seller only when your order is handed to you, and not before.** Do not share it with anyone else or read it out to anyone who contacts you. We will never ask you for your code by text, WhatsApp or phone, other than to the person handing you the package. The driver or seller uses the code to confirm that the right person has the package.\n\nWhen a package is delivered we record **proof of delivery**: the delivery time and place, the code or the person who received it, and any photo or note that our driver takes. For a pickup, the code confirms that you collected it. We use these records to resolve a delivery problem, and they are covered by our Privacy Notice. If you ask someone else to receive the package, they need the code, and you are responsible for sharing it with them.\n\n## Pickup points\n\nA pickup point holds your package for the time shown. Bring the code and, if asked, ID. A package that is not collected in the time may be returned to us. Then we contact you; see \"If nobody is there\" below.\n\n## If nobody is there to receive the delivery\n\nIf the driver cannot hand over your package, for example no one answers, access is not possible, the address is wrong, or the driver feels unsafe, the driver will try to reach you by call and text and wait a short time. If this fails we may reattempt on another day or at another window, ask you to collect from a pickup point, or return the package to us. [[LEGAL: Q21 whether a re-delivery fee or restocking charge applies, and rules for abandoned or unclaimed packages and perishables]] If we cannot deliver after reasonable attempts, we will contact you; for perishable goods that cannot be kept safe, we may not be able to reattempt. We will tell you what we are doing and what, if anything, you are refunded, based on the reason. The delivery is treated as complete if the package is handed over to you or to the person you named or left in a safe place that you asked for, and you accept the risk of a leave-in-place instruction. Please keep your phone on and your delivery instructions up to date. If you paid and nothing was delivered because of us, we refund you.\n\n## Perishable and frozen food\n\nMany pre-orders and runs include fresh, chilled or frozen food. Please:\n\n- Be ready to receive the package in the delivery window, and take it indoors and into the fridge or freezer promptly.\n- Check the package when it arrives: look for spoilage, a broken seal, leaks, a strong smell, warm packaging or a temperature that does not seem right. If in doubt, do not eat it.\n- Report a problem on the day of delivery through Your account > Get help with an order with photos (see the Returns page). Keep the items and packaging until we reply unless unsafe.\n- Allergens and ingredients are on the product label and listing. Check the label.\n\nPerishable items are not accepted back by post, and you will not be asked to return them. Our team will decide each report. We will not deliver perishable items if we think they cannot arrive safely, and we may cancel and refund such items. [[LEGAL: Q13 and Q21 add temperature-holding and food-safety language reviewed against FDA, state and local rules]]\n\n## Seller goods\n\nFor goods from independent sellers, the seller is the seller of the goods. Seller goods may reach you by AfroTransact fulfilment (stock already with us), by the seller''s own delivery, by carrier, or by pickup. For a run, our driver may collect goods from sellers on the route before delivering. The seller is paid after delivery. This does not change your rights against the seller or us.\n\n## Notices and messages\n\nWe announce new windows and runs, reminders of the cutoff, dispatch, confirmation and cancellation through the channels you chose. We send announcements by SMS or WhatsApp only if you opted in. Messages about your own order are order messages. See the SMS and Notification Terms.\n\n## Changes\n\nWe may change how windows and runs work, the places, the fees and the minimums. A change never applies to an order you have already placed, except to fix a problem for you.\n\n## Contact\n\nHelp: Your account > Get help with an order. Phone: {phone}. Email: {legal}. Address: {address}."}'::jsonb, 'New. Explains pre-order windows, delivery runs, delivery fees by method, minimum order counts, cancellation, delivery codes, perishable food and failed deliveries.', now(), 'legal-loader', now(), null
 where not exists (select 1 from legal_version where doc_type = 'preorder-delivery-terms' and (major, minor, patch) >= (1, 0, 0));
update legal_version set effective_date = '2026-12-01'::date, draft_banner = true,
       bodies = '{"en": "# Pre-order and Delivery Run Terms\n\n## What these are\n\nDelivery is expensive when it is one small order to a far place. To keep it fair, we group the orders of one area into one trip. There are two related offers.\n\n- **Pre-order window.** A time window in which you can order products for a set delivery date. When the window closes, the paid orders are delivered, often on a delivery run.\n- **Delivery run.** One planned trip by AfroTransact drivers that brings the orders of one area to their addresses or to pickup points, on a set date. A run is offered only for goods that are already in stock, and only in the places we have switched on.\n\nBoth are ordinary orders with a scheduled delivery. All the Conditions of Use and the Returns, Refunds and Problems With Your Order page apply to them, with the additions below. The offer you see at checkout shows the delivery date, the order cutoff, the fee and how many orders have been placed so far.\n\n## Places we serve\n\nWe start in the US states and cities we have switched on. We offer a run or a window only where the address is inside a covered location. If your address is outside it, we ship by carrier instead, or tell you the order cannot be delivered. Where we serve changes over time. [[LEGAL: Q21 confirm the list of launch states and cities for publication]]\n\n## How you pay\n\nYou are charged like for any other order. At checkout, your card or payment method is authorised for the full amount. We collect the payment for each package when it leaves for you. If a package is cancelled before it leaves, the authorisation is released, so you are not charged; if the money was already collected, it is refunded. Pre-orders and delivery runs never ask for a second payment, and nothing is held back to be charged later. If your payment fails, we release your place in the run. Sales tax and any fee are shown before you place the order. See \"Prices, payment and taxes\" in the Conditions of Use for payment processing by Stripe.\n\n## Order cutoff\n\nEach window and run has a cutoff time. An order placed after the cutoff cannot join it. We show the next open run or window, and if none is open, we say so. An order placed just as the cutoff passes may be refused before you are charged.\n\n## Minimum number of orders\n\nEach window or run has a **minimum number of orders** that we set. We show it at checkout with honest progress, for example \"7 of 10 orders so far\", and we tell you that a run that does not reach its minimum may be cancelled and that you would be refunded in full.\n\n- **If the minimum is reached,** the window or run goes ahead. It may close early once the minimum is reached.\n- **If the end date passes without the minimum,** we make a decision: **cancel** (everyone is refunded) or **proceed** (the orders go ahead as planned). Our team decides, records who decided and why, and tells the customers. Proceeding may mean the delivery date moves, and we tell you if it does.\n- **You can cancel** your own order until its shipment has been prepared, as described in the Returns page.\n\n## If we cancel\n\nIf we cancel a pre-order window or a delivery run, **every order on it is refunded in full, including the delivery fee,** automatically, and the stock is released. If your card was only authorised, the authorisation is released instead, so you are whole either way. You do not have to ask. You will be told by the channels you chose (email, push, and SMS or WhatsApp if you opted in). Refunds appear on your statement according to your bank''s timing. If you paid some of the order with store credit, that part returns as store credit. If only one package of a multi-package order is cancelled, the others are not changed.\n\n## Delivery fees\n\nThe delivery fee depends on the delivery method. The rule that applies to you is shown at checkout, and the amount is recorded on your order. A later change in our fees never changes an order you already placed.\n\n| Method | How the fee is set |\n|---|---|\n| **AfroTransact delivery** (our drivers) | A flat fee set by distance band from the run''s location to your address. Addresses beyond the last band are shipped by carrier instead. |\n| **Carrier shipping** (UPS, USPS, FedEx, DHL Express and others) | The carrier''s rate for the order, or our handling or fallback fee. Some orders over a set value ship free. |\n| **Pickup** (a pickup point, or pickup from the seller) | A pickup fee, which is often zero. |\n\nA window or run can have its own door or pickup fee. A Plus membership can waive the delivery or shipping fee on orders over its minimum (see the Plus Membership Terms). Express options and pickup are not waived. Sales tax may apply to fees where the law says so. [[LEGAL: Q20 confirm]] Fee rules are set by us in our settings and can change; they are never hidden.\n\n## Delivery dates and windows\n\nThe delivery date is our plan, and the delivery window (for example, morning or afternoon) is our best estimate. We do not promise a time. Weather, traffic, vehicle problems, a closed road, safety, the seller''s stock or events outside our control may move a date. We tell you as soon as we can by your notification channels, and if the new date does not work, you can cancel the shipment if it has not been prepared. If we cannot deliver within a reasonable time after the date we gave, contact us through Your account > Get help with an order. [[LEGAL: Q30 confirm delay-notice and cancel-and-refund rules for pre-paid orders under the FTC Mail, Internet or Telephone Order Merchandise Rule and state law]]\n\n## Delivery codes and proof of delivery\n\nEach order that we deliver or that you collect has a **delivery code** (handover code) in your order page and your messages. **Give the code to the driver or seller only when your order is handed to you, and not before.** Do not share it with anyone else or read it out to anyone who contacts you. We will never ask you for your code by text, WhatsApp or phone, other than to the person handing you the package. The driver or seller uses the code to confirm that the right person has the package.\n\nWhen a package is delivered we record **proof of delivery**: the delivery time and place, the code or the person who received it, and any photo or note that our driver takes. For a pickup, the code confirms that you collected it. We use these records to resolve a delivery problem, and they are covered by our Privacy Notice. If you ask someone else to receive the package, they need the code, and you are responsible for sharing it with them.\n\n## Pickup points\n\nA pickup point holds your package for the time shown. Bring the code and, if asked, ID. A package that is not collected in the time may be returned to us. Then we contact you; see \"If nobody is there\" below.\n\n## If nobody is there to receive the delivery\n\nIf the driver cannot hand over your package, for example no one answers, access is not possible, the address is wrong, or the driver feels unsafe, the driver will try to reach you by call and text and wait a short time. If this fails we may reattempt on another day or at another window, ask you to collect from a pickup point, or return the package to us. [[LEGAL: Q21 whether a re-delivery fee or restocking charge applies, and rules for abandoned or unclaimed packages and perishables]] If we cannot deliver after reasonable attempts, we will contact you; for perishable goods that cannot be kept safe, we may not be able to reattempt. We will tell you what we are doing and what, if anything, you are refunded, based on the reason. The delivery is treated as complete if the package is handed over to you or to the person you named or left in a safe place that you asked for, and you accept the risk of a leave-in-place instruction. Please keep your phone on and your delivery instructions up to date. If you paid and nothing was delivered because of us, we refund you.\n\n## Perishable and frozen food\n\nMany pre-orders and runs include fresh, chilled or frozen food. Please:\n\n- Be ready to receive the package in the delivery window, and take it indoors and into the fridge or freezer promptly.\n- Check the package when it arrives: look for spoilage, a broken seal, leaks, a strong smell, warm packaging or a temperature that does not seem right. If in doubt, do not eat it.\n- Report a problem on the day of delivery through Your account > Get help with an order with photos (see the Returns page). Keep the items and packaging until we reply unless unsafe.\n- Allergens and ingredients are on the product label and listing. Check the label.\n\nPerishable items are not accepted back by post, and you will not be asked to return them. Our team will decide each report. We will not deliver perishable items if we think they cannot arrive safely, and we may cancel and refund such items. [[LEGAL: Q13 and Q21 add temperature-holding and food-safety language reviewed against FDA, state and local rules]]\n\n## Seller goods\n\nFor goods from independent sellers, the seller is the seller of the goods. Seller goods may reach you by AfroTransact fulfilment (stock already with us), by the seller''s own delivery, by carrier, or by pickup. For a run, our driver may collect goods from sellers on the route before delivering. The seller is paid after delivery. This does not change your rights against the seller or us.\n\n## Notices and messages\n\nWe announce new windows and runs, reminders of the cutoff, dispatch, confirmation and cancellation through the channels you chose. We send announcements by SMS or WhatsApp only if you opted in. Messages about your own order are order messages. See the SMS and Notification Terms.\n\n## Changes\n\nWe may change how windows and runs work, the places, the fees and the minimums. A change never applies to an order you have already placed, except to fix a problem for you.\n\n## Contact\n\nHelp: Your account > Get help with an order. Phone: {phone}. Email: {legal}. Address: {address}."}'::jsonb, change_summary = 'New. Explains pre-order windows, delivery runs, delivery fees by method, minimum order counts, cancellation, delivery codes, perishable food and failed deliveries.', created_at = now(), updated_at = now()
    where doc_type = 'preorder-delivery-terms' and (major, minor, patch) = (1, 0, 0) and status = 'CURRENT'
      and created_by in ('seed', 'legal-loader') and updated_at = created_at;

-- community-guidelines 1.0 (effective 2026-12-01; locales: en; draft banner on)
delete from legal_version where doc_type = 'community-guidelines' and created_by = 'seed'
    and exists (select 1 from legal_version c where c.doc_type = 'community-guidelines' and c.status = 'CURRENT'
                and c.created_by = 'seed' and c.updated_at = c.created_at and (c.major, c.minor, c.patch) > (1, 0, 0));
update legal_version set status = 'ARCHIVED', archived_at = now(), updated_at = now()
    where doc_type = 'community-guidelines' and status = 'CURRENT' and (major, minor, patch) < (1, 0, 0);
insert into legal_version (id, doc_type, version, major, minor, patch, effective_date, status, draft_banner, bodies,
                           change_summary, created_at, created_by, updated_at, archived_at)
select '3eeac5f5-bf5f-5db5-8d74-1c3302be7170'::uuid, 'community-guidelines', '1.0', 1, 0, 0, '2026-12-01'::date, 'CURRENT', true,
       '{"en": "# Community Guidelines\n\n## Why these rules exist\n\nReviews, photos and messages help people buy with confidence and help sellers improve. They only work if they are honest and respectful. These guidelines are part of the Conditions of Use. Breaking them can lead to content being removed and, for serious or repeated cases, to limits on or closure of an account.\n\n## Reviews and ratings\n\n### Who can review\n\n- **Verified purchase only.** You can review a product only if you received it: you need a delivered order for that product. Your review shows a \"Verified purchase\" label. Bookings can be reviewed after the service by the person who booked it.\n- **One review per product.** You can post one review per product. You can edit your review for 30 days after you post it. After that it is final. You can delete your review at any time.\n- If we cannot check your purchase, for example because of a system problem, we will ask you to try again, and we will not guess.\n\n### What a good review is\n\nSay what you bought, what you liked and what you did not, and how it was. You can add a title, text of up to 4,000 characters and up to 5 photos. Photos must be yours, of the item you received. Your review shows your first name and the first letter of your last name (for example \"Adaeze N.\"). Nothing else about you is shown.\n\n### What is not allowed\n\n- **Fake or misleading reviews:** reviews by someone who did not buy or use the item, reviews written by or for the seller, their staff, family or competitors, reviews bought or traded, or reviews written by an AI tool and presented as your own experience.\n- **Incentivised reviews:** reviews in exchange for money, free goods, credit, discounts, gifts or other rewards, or any promise of a better rating. Sellers must not offer anything for a review or ask for only positive ones, and must not ask a customer to change or remove a review. If a seller gave you a free product or other reward, do not review it here. (Referral and other AfroTransact program rewards are for referring friends, never for reviews.)\n- **Review gating or suppression:** asking only happy customers to review, or threats and pressure to remove a review.\n- Personal information of anyone (names, phone numbers, emails, addresses), links, contact details or ads.\n- Hate speech, harassment, threats, sexual content, graphic violence, discrimination or abuse of any person or group.\n- Content that infringes someone else''s rights, or that breaks the law, or that is about a delivery or customer service experience that has nothing to do with the product (these are better reported to support).\n- Spam, repeated text, off-topic content, and attempts to manipulate ratings.\n\nYou can say that a product was poor. You can''t make false statements of fact about a seller or provider.\n\n### How we check\n\nWe check every review by machine for things like bad language, links, email addresses and phone numbers. A review with none of these flags is published straight away. A flagged review is held and a member of our team reviews it, and may approve it, reject it with a reason, or remove it. If a review is rejected, you are told why and can edit it and send it again. Reasons include abusive content, personal information, spam, off-topic content, conflict of interest and other reasons. We may also remove a review later if we learn it breaks these guidelines. We do not remove a review because it is negative, and we do not remove reviews at the request of a seller unless it breaks these rules.\n\n### Reporting a review\n\nUse **Report** on any review to tell us why it breaks these guidelines. We review reports and take action. Reports are looked at by our team; a report is not a guarantee that a review will be removed.\n\n### Seller replies\n\nThe seller of a product can post a public reply to a review. Replies must follow the same rules: be polite, factual and about the product or the experience, and not include personal information of the reviewer or offers of a reward for changing the review. A seller may report a review they think breaks these guidelines. Sellers cannot edit or delete your review.\n\n[[LEGAL: Q25 check review practices against the FTC rule on fake reviews and testimonials (16 CFR Part 465), the Consumer Review Fairness Act, and state laws, and decide the wording for moderation and removal; confirm whether reviews of the platform''s own AfroTransact Retail products need a disclosure of the relationship]]\n\n## Messages with sellers, providers, drivers and support\n\nMessages on AfroTransact are for your orders, bookings and deliveries. Please be respectful and honest. You may not:\n\n- Harass, threaten, insult or discriminate against anyone.\n- Ask for or send personal, payment or banking details outside the way our checkout works, or ask someone to pay or deal off AfroTransact to avoid fees or protections.\n- Send spam, ads, scams, malware or links that are not about the order.\n- Share the delivery code with anyone other than the person handing over your package.\n- Pretend to be someone else, including AfroTransact staff.\n- Share another person''s private information or photos without their permission.\n- Send sexual content, or content that is illegal.\n\nWe can see messages sent through AfroTransact and may review them to resolve problems, prevent fraud and enforce these rules. See the Privacy Notice. If you feel unsafe, contact local emergency services first and then report to us.\n\nSellers, providers and drivers follow rules at least as strict as these in their own agreements.\n\n## Using Lola, our AI shopping assistant\n\nLola is an AI assistant. It can help you find products, track a package, change delivery instructions and get help with an order, and it will ask you to confirm important actions.\n\n- **Lola is a machine and can be wrong.** Check important details, such as price, delivery date, ingredients and allergens, on the product page or label. Do not rely on Lola for medical, legal, tax, financial or immigration advice.\n- **Do not put sensitive information in a chat:** health details, government ID numbers, full card numbers or bank details, or other people''s private details. Lola tries to mask personal details before it sends text to a model, but you should not rely on that.\n- **Use Lola fairly.** Don''t use it to try to break our systems, to get others'' account information, to make prohibited items, to harass or to produce harmful content, to extract Lola''s instructions, or to run automated or high-volume requests. Don''t use Lola to write fake reviews.\n- Lola can hand over to a person if needed, with a short, masked summary.\n- Lola''s answers are not an offer or a promise by AfroTransact. A price or policy that Lola states does not override the product page or our written terms. You can ask Lola to start a request to a person at any time.\n- Lola chats are handled under the Privacy Notice. AI features rely on model providers; please see that notice.\n\n[[LEGAL: Q16 add any AI-disclosure and chatbot-disclosure text required by state law (for example California bot disclosure, Utah AI disclosure and Colorado AI Act), and confirm the statement about human hand-off]]\n\n## Reporting and enforcement\n\nIf you see something that breaks these guidelines, use **Report** on the page or email {legal}. We may remove content, warn you, limit what you can post, cancel an order, withhold rewards, or suspend or close an account, depending on how serious or repeated the breach is. We try to be fair and tell you why where we can. You can ask us to review a decision by replying to our message or through Your account > Get help with an order. Reports about intellectual property go through the Intellectual Property and Copyright Policy.\n\n## Changes\n\nWe update these guidelines from time to time. The version and effective date are at the top of this page."}'::jsonb, 'New. Rules for reviews and ratings, messages with sellers, providers and drivers, and use of the Lola AI assistant.', now(), 'legal-loader', now(), null
 where not exists (select 1 from legal_version where doc_type = 'community-guidelines' and (major, minor, patch) >= (1, 0, 0));
update legal_version set effective_date = '2026-12-01'::date, draft_banner = true,
       bodies = '{"en": "# Community Guidelines\n\n## Why these rules exist\n\nReviews, photos and messages help people buy with confidence and help sellers improve. They only work if they are honest and respectful. These guidelines are part of the Conditions of Use. Breaking them can lead to content being removed and, for serious or repeated cases, to limits on or closure of an account.\n\n## Reviews and ratings\n\n### Who can review\n\n- **Verified purchase only.** You can review a product only if you received it: you need a delivered order for that product. Your review shows a \"Verified purchase\" label. Bookings can be reviewed after the service by the person who booked it.\n- **One review per product.** You can post one review per product. You can edit your review for 30 days after you post it. After that it is final. You can delete your review at any time.\n- If we cannot check your purchase, for example because of a system problem, we will ask you to try again, and we will not guess.\n\n### What a good review is\n\nSay what you bought, what you liked and what you did not, and how it was. You can add a title, text of up to 4,000 characters and up to 5 photos. Photos must be yours, of the item you received. Your review shows your first name and the first letter of your last name (for example \"Adaeze N.\"). Nothing else about you is shown.\n\n### What is not allowed\n\n- **Fake or misleading reviews:** reviews by someone who did not buy or use the item, reviews written by or for the seller, their staff, family or competitors, reviews bought or traded, or reviews written by an AI tool and presented as your own experience.\n- **Incentivised reviews:** reviews in exchange for money, free goods, credit, discounts, gifts or other rewards, or any promise of a better rating. Sellers must not offer anything for a review or ask for only positive ones, and must not ask a customer to change or remove a review. If a seller gave you a free product or other reward, do not review it here. (Referral and other AfroTransact program rewards are for referring friends, never for reviews.)\n- **Review gating or suppression:** asking only happy customers to review, or threats and pressure to remove a review.\n- Personal information of anyone (names, phone numbers, emails, addresses), links, contact details or ads.\n- Hate speech, harassment, threats, sexual content, graphic violence, discrimination or abuse of any person or group.\n- Content that infringes someone else''s rights, or that breaks the law, or that is about a delivery or customer service experience that has nothing to do with the product (these are better reported to support).\n- Spam, repeated text, off-topic content, and attempts to manipulate ratings.\n\nYou can say that a product was poor. You can''t make false statements of fact about a seller or provider.\n\n### How we check\n\nWe check every review by machine for things like bad language, links, email addresses and phone numbers. A review with none of these flags is published straight away. A flagged review is held and a member of our team reviews it, and may approve it, reject it with a reason, or remove it. If a review is rejected, you are told why and can edit it and send it again. Reasons include abusive content, personal information, spam, off-topic content, conflict of interest and other reasons. We may also remove a review later if we learn it breaks these guidelines. We do not remove a review because it is negative, and we do not remove reviews at the request of a seller unless it breaks these rules.\n\n### Reporting a review\n\nUse **Report** on any review to tell us why it breaks these guidelines. We review reports and take action. Reports are looked at by our team; a report is not a guarantee that a review will be removed.\n\n### Seller replies\n\nThe seller of a product can post a public reply to a review. Replies must follow the same rules: be polite, factual and about the product or the experience, and not include personal information of the reviewer or offers of a reward for changing the review. A seller may report a review they think breaks these guidelines. Sellers cannot edit or delete your review.\n\n[[LEGAL: Q25 check review practices against the FTC rule on fake reviews and testimonials (16 CFR Part 465), the Consumer Review Fairness Act, and state laws, and decide the wording for moderation and removal; confirm whether reviews of the platform''s own AfroTransact Retail products need a disclosure of the relationship]]\n\n## Messages with sellers, providers, drivers and support\n\nMessages on AfroTransact are for your orders, bookings and deliveries. Please be respectful and honest. You may not:\n\n- Harass, threaten, insult or discriminate against anyone.\n- Ask for or send personal, payment or banking details outside the way our checkout works, or ask someone to pay or deal off AfroTransact to avoid fees or protections.\n- Send spam, ads, scams, malware or links that are not about the order.\n- Share the delivery code with anyone other than the person handing over your package.\n- Pretend to be someone else, including AfroTransact staff.\n- Share another person''s private information or photos without their permission.\n- Send sexual content, or content that is illegal.\n\nWe can see messages sent through AfroTransact and may review them to resolve problems, prevent fraud and enforce these rules. See the Privacy Notice. If you feel unsafe, contact local emergency services first and then report to us.\n\nSellers, providers and drivers follow rules at least as strict as these in their own agreements.\n\n## Using Lola, our AI shopping assistant\n\nLola is an AI assistant. It can help you find products, track a package, change delivery instructions and get help with an order, and it will ask you to confirm important actions.\n\n- **Lola is a machine and can be wrong.** Check important details, such as price, delivery date, ingredients and allergens, on the product page or label. Do not rely on Lola for medical, legal, tax, financial or immigration advice.\n- **Do not put sensitive information in a chat:** health details, government ID numbers, full card numbers or bank details, or other people''s private details. Lola tries to mask personal details before it sends text to a model, but you should not rely on that.\n- **Use Lola fairly.** Don''t use it to try to break our systems, to get others'' account information, to make prohibited items, to harass or to produce harmful content, to extract Lola''s instructions, or to run automated or high-volume requests. Don''t use Lola to write fake reviews.\n- Lola can hand over to a person if needed, with a short, masked summary.\n- Lola''s answers are not an offer or a promise by AfroTransact. A price or policy that Lola states does not override the product page or our written terms. You can ask Lola to start a request to a person at any time.\n- Lola chats are handled under the Privacy Notice. AI features rely on model providers; please see that notice.\n\n[[LEGAL: Q16 add any AI-disclosure and chatbot-disclosure text required by state law (for example California bot disclosure, Utah AI disclosure and Colorado AI Act), and confirm the statement about human hand-off]]\n\n## Reporting and enforcement\n\nIf you see something that breaks these guidelines, use **Report** on the page or email {legal}. We may remove content, warn you, limit what you can post, cancel an order, withhold rewards, or suspend or close an account, depending on how serious or repeated the breach is. We try to be fair and tell you why where we can. You can ask us to review a decision by replying to our message or through Your account > Get help with an order. Reports about intellectual property go through the Intellectual Property and Copyright Policy.\n\n## Changes\n\nWe update these guidelines from time to time. The version and effective date are at the top of this page."}'::jsonb, change_summary = 'New. Rules for reviews and ratings, messages with sellers, providers and drivers, and use of the Lola AI assistant.', created_at = now(), updated_at = now()
    where doc_type = 'community-guidelines' and (major, minor, patch) = (1, 0, 0) and status = 'CURRENT'
      and created_by in ('seed', 'legal-loader') and updated_at = created_at;

-- ip-policy 1.0 (effective 2026-12-01; locales: en; draft banner on)
delete from legal_version where doc_type = 'ip-policy' and created_by = 'seed'
    and exists (select 1 from legal_version c where c.doc_type = 'ip-policy' and c.status = 'CURRENT'
                and c.created_by = 'seed' and c.updated_at = c.created_at and (c.major, c.minor, c.patch) > (1, 0, 0));
update legal_version set status = 'ARCHIVED', archived_at = now(), updated_at = now()
    where doc_type = 'ip-policy' and status = 'CURRENT' and (major, minor, patch) < (1, 0, 0);
insert into legal_version (id, doc_type, version, major, minor, patch, effective_date, status, draft_banner, bodies,
                           change_summary, created_at, created_by, updated_at, archived_at)
select '7e7bf89c-831d-5f09-aed0-003849c16ff7'::uuid, 'ip-policy', '1.0', 1, 0, 0, '2026-12-01'::date, 'CURRENT', true,
       '{"en": "# Intellectual Property and Copyright Policy\n\n## Our approach\n\nWe respect the rights of creators, brands and owners and expect sellers, providers and customers to do the same. We do not allow counterfeit goods or content that infringes someone else''s copyright, trademark or other rights. The Prohibited and Restricted Items policy lists counterfeit goods among the things that are never allowed.\n\nThis policy is for reporting. It is not legal advice, and you should talk to a lawyer if you are unsure whether your rights are infringed.\n\n## Reporting copyright infringement (DMCA notice)\n\nIf you believe that content on AfroTransact infringes your copyright, send a written notice to our designated agent. Under the US Digital Millennium Copyright Act (17 U.S.C. section 512), your notice must include:\n\n1. Your physical or electronic **signature** (or that of a person authorised to act for the owner).\n2. A description of the **copyrighted work** that you say is infringed (or, for many works on one site, a representative list).\n3. A description of the **material you say infringes**, and where it is on AfroTransact, with enough detail for us to find it (for example, the web address of the listing).\n4. Your **name, address, telephone number and email address.**\n5. A statement that you have a **good-faith belief** that the use is not authorised by the copyright owner, its agent or the law.\n6. A statement that **the information in your notice is accurate and, under penalty of perjury, that you are the owner or authorised to act for the owner** of the right allegedly infringed.\n\n**Our designated agent:**\n\n[[LEGAL: Q07 name of designated agent, postal address, telephone, email, and confirm that the agent has been registered with the US Copyright Office''s DMCA designated agent directory, with the renewal date every three years]]\n\nYou can also use the **Report** link on a listing and email {legal}. A report that is missing the items above may not be enough for us to act on it, but we may still act on it under our other rules.\n\n**Be careful:** under section 512(f), a person who knowingly and materially misrepresents that material is infringing, or that it was removed by mistake, can be liable for damages. Please consider fair use and other exceptions before you send a notice.\n\n## What we do when we receive a notice\n\nIf a notice is complete, we act promptly. We may remove or disable access to the material and tell the person who posted it (the seller, provider or customer) that we did so, and we may send them a copy of your notice, including your name and contact details. We may also take action on the account under the repeat infringer rules. We may share your notice with the person who posted the content and publish it in a database of takedown notices.\n\n## Counter-notice (if your content was removed)\n\nIf you believe that your content was removed by mistake or misidentification, you can send a counter-notice to the designated agent above. It must include:\n\n1. Your physical or electronic **signature.**\n2. Identification of the material that was removed and **where it appeared** before it was removed.\n3. A statement, **under penalty of perjury, that you have a good-faith belief** that the material was removed because of mistake or misidentification.\n4. Your **name, address and telephone number,** and a statement that you **consent to the jurisdiction of the federal court** for the district where your address is (or, if you are outside the United States, any district where we can be found), and that you **will accept service of process** from the person who sent the notice or their agent.\n\nWhen we receive a valid counter-notice, we send a copy to the person who sent the original notice and tell them that we will restore the material in **10 business days** unless they tell us within that time that they have filed a court action against you. If they do not, we may restore the material **no sooner than 10 and no later than 14 business days** after we receive the counter-notice. [[LEGAL: Q07 confirm the safe-harbour timelines and wording]]\n\n## Repeat infringers\n\nWe will end the accounts of users and sellers who are repeat infringers, in appropriate circumstances. We treat an account as a repeat infringer when it has received [[LEGAL: Q26 repeat-infringer threshold, for example three valid notices not successfully counter-noticed within 12 months]]. We may also suspend or limit an account, hold payouts as our agreements allow, and remove listings on a first valid report if the infringement is clear or serious (for example counterfeit goods). We apply this policy fairly and consistently, and we may change the thresholds.\n\n## Reporting trademark infringement and counterfeits\n\nIf you own a trademark and believe a listing or other content is counterfeit or uses your mark in a way that is likely to confuse customers, send a report to {legal} or use **Report** on the listing. Please include:\n\n- Your name, company and contact details, and your relationship to the brand (owner or authorised agent);\n- The trademark, with the registration number and registry (for example, the USPTO), and proof of rights if we ask;\n- The link or listing ID and a description of why the item is counterfeit or infringing, with photos or other evidence where you can;\n- A statement that you have a good-faith belief that the use is not authorised and that your report is accurate.\n\nWe review trademark and counterfeit reports promptly, and may remove the listing, cancel orders, refund buyers in full, suspend the seller, and share information with the rights owner and law enforcement where the law allows. We may ask the seller to respond or give proof (such as invoices or an authorisation to sell). Genuine resale of authentic goods (\"first sale\") and fair use of a brand name to describe a product can be lawful, so we may ask the seller for proof before we decide.\n\nWe do not decide trademark ownership. If both sides disagree, we may restore a listing if the reporter doesn''t take legal action within a reasonable time. [[LEGAL: Q26 decide the trademark dispute process, the time limit and whether to offer a brand registry]]\n\n## Other intellectual property\n\nFor reports about other rights (for example design rights, patents, trade secrets, or the right of publicity such as someone''s image or voice), write to {legal} with the details. We may need a court order or proof.\n\n## If you bought a counterfeit item\n\nIf you think an item you bought is counterfeit, report it through Your account > Get help with an order (see the Returns, Refunds and Problems With Your Order page). Our team will decide the outcome and a refund is made to the payers as described there. Please keep the item and its packaging.\n\n## Our own rights\n\nAfroTransact''s name, logos, designs and software are ours or our licensors''. Do not use them without written permission. See the Conditions of Use.\n\n## Contact\n\nDesignated agent: see above. General legal: {legal}. Address: {address}."}'::jsonb, 'New. How to report copyright, trademark and counterfeit problems, how counter-notices work, and how we treat repeat infringers.', now(), 'legal-loader', now(), null
 where not exists (select 1 from legal_version where doc_type = 'ip-policy' and (major, minor, patch) >= (1, 0, 0));
update legal_version set effective_date = '2026-12-01'::date, draft_banner = true,
